{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c437","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ceca-cad7-7401-b120-5d187a59f4b1"},"sequence":118,"recorded_at":1780531400000231,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f679b6f1-9902-47f8-8dc1-d6bbf0923c83","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"f679b6f1-9902-47f8-8dc1-d6bbf0923c83","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f679b6f1-9902-47f8-8dc1-d6bbf0923c83"},"call_id":"call_01a0cecb118c738aa377a7ec3eea19b1","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`.\n(10547 line(s) above)\n10548|#### 13.14.2 Fidelity, projection, and lineage\n10549|\n10550|The dispositions are <code>exact|semantic|summarized|opaque_preserved|synthesized|omitted|unrecoverable</code>.\n10551|Every non-exact row names one or more of the closed core reasons\n10552|<code>target_no_equivalent|source_not_persisted|source_truncated|source_corrupt|foreign_encrypted_payload|foreign_signature_unverifiable|target_schema_constraint|target_context_limit|target_size_limit|target_version_gate|official_importer_loss|graph_flattened|unsafe_pending_action|credential_excluded|secret_policy|operator_policy|unsupported_media_type|unknown_native_event|derived_index_rebuilt</code>,\n10553|or a reverse-DNS extension reason that cannot redefine a core code.\n10554|Every captured candidate reconciles once to raw evidence or exclusion; every\n10555|raw item to a canonical item or normalization disposition; every canonical\n10556|item to staged/live target evidence or a target disposition. Fidelity Report\n10557|1.0.0 records archive/target scope, profile, tuples, per-item mappings, counts\n10558|by kind/block/bytes/disposition/reason, completeness, semantic continuity,\n10559|native resumability, evidence IDs, and extensions. An aggregate score cannot\n10560|replace item gates.\n10561|\n10562|Profiles are <code>strict_exact|maximal_safe|compact|messages_only|archive_only</code>;\n10563|maximal-safe is default. Strategies are\n10564|<code>same_environment_native_rewrite|target_native_writer|target_official_import|continuation_context|archive_only</code>.\n10565|Continuation context is explicitly non-native historical fidelity.\n10566|\n10567|Projection Plan 1.0.0 binds operation/bundle, Capture/Canonical inputs,\n10568|source/target tuples, expected new native ID, strategy/profile, ordered\n10569|item mappings and reasons, target operations/resources, exclusions, limits,\n10570|<code>fidelity_basis_digest</code>, and extensions. It never predicts a final\n10571|Fidelity Report ID. Clone Projected Object Manifest 1.0.0 binds plan and target\n10572|ID to sorted disjoint blob/directory entries partitioned by operation sequence.\n10573|It grants no live authority and cannot populate a Checkpoint.\n10574|\n10575|Clone Read-Back Evidence Manifest 1.0.0 binds operation,\n10576|<code>staged|live</code>, plan/projected manifest, equal expected/observed\n10577|native IDs, target tuple, parsed count/heads, Workspace Binding, structural\n10578|digest, and sorted evidence blobs. Modes cannot be relabeled. Clone Validation\n10579|Report 1.0.0 aggregates both reads, identity/workspace/marker/resume checks,\n10580|Fidelity Report, findings, and valid result; every applicable check must pass.\n10581|\n10582|Migration Checkpoint 1.0.0 binds operation/bundle, source snapshot and optional\n10583|AX Checkpoint, Canonical Session, Projection Plan, tuples, previous checkpoint/\n10584|receipt, policy and fidelity-basis hashes, visible low-authority projection,\n10585|and extensions. It does not name the final report. Visible text comes from\n10586|typed escaped fields and is user context, never an assistant reply or control\n10587|instruction.\n10588|\n10589|Clone Lineage Receipt 1.0.0 binds source/target identities and tuples,\n10590|Migration Checkpoint, Projection Plan, G3, final reports, Provider commit fact,\n10591|target Checkpoint, committed event, and optional prior receipt. It names G3,\n10592|never G4; G4 names it. Lineage is descriptive, never authorization.\n10593|\n10594|The following are the complete closed schemas for those contracts.\n10595|\n10596|<code>FidelityCounts</code> contains exactly the seven uint53 members\n10597|<code>exact</code>, <code>semantic</code>, <code>summarized</code>,\n10598|<code>opaque_preserved</code>, <code>synthesized</code>, <code>omitted</code>,\n10599|and <code>unrecoverable</code>.\n10600|\n10601|<code>FidelityDispositionRecord</code> contains exactly\n10602|<code>source_item_key:string[1..512]</code>,\n10603|<code>source_class:string[1..128]</code>,\n10604|<code>source_evidence_ids:sorted unique digest[1..65536]</code>,\n10605|<code>canonical_object_id:digest|null</code>,\n10606|<code>target_locator:string[1..1024]|null</code>,\n10607|<code>disposition:exact|semantic|summarized|opaque_preserved|synthesized|omitted|unrecoverable</code>,\n10608|<code>reason_codes:sorted unique string[1..128][0..128]</code>,\n10609|<code>explanation:string[1..4096]</code>,\n10610|<code>staged_evidence_object_ids:sorted unique digest[0..65536]</code>,\n10611|<code>live_evidence_object_ids:sorted unique digest[0..65536]</code>, and\n10612|<code>extensions</code>. Exact requires an empty reason set; every other\n10613|disposition requires at least one reason. Synthesized requires no source\n10614|canonical object; every non-synthesized row traces to captured source evidence.\n10615|\n10616|Fidelity Report 1.0.0 contains exactly:\n10617|\n10618|| Field | Type and constraint |\n10619|| --- | --- |\n10620|| <code>schema</code> / <code>schema_version</code> | Exact <code>urn:ax:schema:fidelity-report</code> / <code>1.0.0</code> |\n10621|| <code>fidelity_report_id</code> | JCS digest with only this member omitted |\n10622|| <code>scope</code> | <code>archive&#124;target</code> |\n10623|| <code>operation_id</code> / <code>bundle_id</code> | UUIDv7 operation / bundle chain |\n10624|| <code>source_snapshot_digest</code> | Terminal captured snapshot digest |\n10625|| <code>capture_manifest_id</code> / <code>canonical_session_id</code> | Exact lower immutable inputs |\n10626|| <code>projection_plan_id</code> | digest or null; null exactly for archive |\n10627|| <code>source_environment</code> | Exact source tuple |\n10628|| <code>target_environment</code> | Exact target tuple or null; null exactly for archive |\n10629|| <code>profile</code> | Closed fidelity profile; <code>archive_only</code> exactly for archive |\n10630|| <code>required_dispositions</code> | Closed map from class to sorted unique non-empty disposition sets |\n10631|| <code>forbid_reasons</code> | Sorted unique string[1..128][0..128] |\n10632|| <code>dispositions</code> | <code>FidelityDispositionRecord[1..1000000]</code>, sorted unique by source item key with synthesized rows ordered after source rows |\n10633|| <code>counts</code> | Exact <code>FidelityCounts</code>, derived from disposition rows |\n10634|| <code>event_kind_counts</code> | Closed map of every Canonical Event kind to <code>FidelityCounts</code> |\n10635|| <code>content_block_counts</code> | Closed map of every content-block type to <code>FidelityCounts</code> |\n10636|| <code>byte_counts</code> | Closed map of every disposition to uint53 |\n10637|| <code>reason_counts</code> | Sorted map string[1..128] to uint53&gt;0 |\n10638|| <code>raw_bundle_complete</code> / <code>canonical_complete</code> | Core-derived booleans |\n10639|| <code>target_semantically_continuable</code> / <code>target_natively_resumable</code> | Core-derived booleans; both false for archive |\n10640|| <code>staged_read_back_evidence_manifest_id</code> / <code>live_read_back_evidence_manifest_id</code> | digest or null; both null for archive and both non-null for target |\n10641|| <code>adapter_attestations</code> | Sorted unique digest[0..64], evidence only |\n10642|| <code>extensions</code> | Reverse-DNS keys only |\n10643|\n10644|Every Capture Manifest item and Canonical Event occurs in exactly one\n10645|non-synthesized disposition row. Aggregate maps reconcile exactly to the rows\n10646|and cannot replace them. A target report does not name Clone Validation Report,\n10647|Lineage Receipt, G4, or a future event. An archive report references only the\n10648|G0/G1 closure and is therefore targetless.\n10649|\n10650|Projection Plan 1.0.0 contains exactly:\n10651|\n10652|| Field | Type and constraint |\n10653|| --- | --- |\n10654|| <code>schema</code> / <code>schema_version</code> | Exact <code>urn:ax:schema:projection-plan</code> / <code>1.0.0</code> |\n10655|| <code>projection_plan_id</code> | JCS digest with only this member omitted |\n10656|| <code>operation_id</code> / <code>bundle_id</code> | UUIDv7 operation / bundle chain |\n10657|| <code>request_digest</code> / <code>source_snapshot_digest</code> | Terminal canonical request/snapshot digests |\n10658|| <code>capture_manifest_id</code> / <code>canonical_session_id</code> | Exact lower inputs |\n10659|| <code>canonical_event_ids</code> | Ordered unique digest[0..65536], equal to Canonical Session order |\n10660|| <code>source_environment</code> / <code>target_environment</code> | Exact tuples |\n10661|| <code>expected_target_native_session_id</code> | Newly allocated string[1..512] |\n10662|| <code>target_workspace</code> | Exact <code>WorkspaceBinding</code> |\n10663|| <code>strategy</code> | <code>same_environment_native_rewrite&#124;target_native_writer&#124;target_official_import&#124;continuation_context</code> |\n10664|| <code>strategy_rationale</code> | string[1..4096] |\n10665|| <code>fidelity_profile</code> | <code>strict_exact&#124;maximal_safe&#124;compact&#124;messages_only</code> |\n10666|| <code>required_dispositions</code> / <code>forbid_reasons</code> | Exact policy from request |\n10667|| <code>item_mappings</code> | <code>ProjectionItemMapping[1..1000000]</code>, one for every captured/canonical item |\n10668|| <code>target_operations</code> | <code>ProjectionTargetOperation[1..65536]</code>, ordered by sequence |\n10669|| <code>expected_resources</code> | <code>ExpectedTargetResource[0..65536]</code>, sorted by operation sequence/key |\n10670|| <code>synthesized_events</code> | <code>SynthesizedProjectionEvent[0..65536]</code>, ordered by insertion sequence |\n10671|| <code>security_exclusions</code> | Sorted unique capture-class[0..9] |\n10672|| <code>resource_limits</code> | Exact <code>ResourceLimits</code> |\n10673|| <code>transaction_plan</code> / <code>read_back_plan</code> / <code>resume_plan</code> / <code>rollback_plan</code> | Closed plan components below |\n10674|| <code>required_contracts</code> | Sorted unique <code>ContractRequirement[1..64]</code> |\n10675|| <code>required_capabilities</code> | Sorted unique string[1..128][1..64] |\n10676|| <code>fidelity_basis_digest</code> | Terminal digest of item mappings, policy, and predicted counts; never a report locator |\n10677|| <code>source_adapter_build_digest</code> / <code>target_adapter_build_digest</code> / <code>controller_build_digest</code> | Host-observed digests |\n10678|| <code>extensions</code> | Reverse-DNS keys only |\n10679|\n10680|<code>ProjectionItemMapping</code> contains exactly\n10681|<code>source_item_key:string[1..512]</code>,\n10682|<code>canonical_object_id:digest|null</code>,\n10683|<code>target_resource_keys:sorted unique string[1..512][0..65536]</code>,\n10684|<code>expected_disposition:fidelity-disposition</code>,\n10685|<code>reason_codes:sorted unique string[1..128][0..128]</code>, and\n10686|<code>extensions</code>. <code>ProjectionTargetOperation</code> contains\n10687|exactly <code>sequence:uint53&gt;0</code>,\n10688|<code>action:create_directory|write_blob|write_native_record|rebuild_index</code>,\n10689|<code>resource_keys:sorted unique string[1..512][1..65536]</code>,\n10690|<code>depends_on_sequences:sorted unique uint53[0..65536]</code>, and\n10691|<code>extensions</code>. Dependencies are lower sequences and form a DAG.\n10692|<code>ExpectedTargetResource</code> contains exactly\n10693|<code>operation_sequence:uint53&gt;0</code>, <code>resource_key:string[1..512]</code>,\n10694|<code>kind:blob|directory</code>, <code>mode:uint32[0..4095]|null</code>,\n10695|<code>expected_blob_id:digest|null</code>, and <code>extensions</code>; blob and\n10696|directory nullability is branch-exact.\n10697|<code>SynthesizedProjectionEvent</code> contains exactly\n10698|<code>canonical_event_id:digest</code>,\n10699|<code>insertion_after_event_id:digest|null</code>,\n10700|<code>purpose:migration_checkpoint|summary|delimiter</code>, and\n10701|<code>extensions</code>.\n10702|\n10703|<code>TransactionPlan</code> contains exactly\n10704|<code>materialization_intent=clone</code>,\n10705|<code>target_collision_policy=must_be_absent</code>,\n10706|<code>activation=dormant_validated</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n10707|<code>ReadBackPlan</code> contains exactly\n10708|<code>modes:[staged,live]</code>,\n10709|<code>require_identity_match=true</code>,\n10710|<code>require_workspace_match=true</code>,\n10711|<code>require_semantic_marker=true</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n10712|<code>ResumeProjectionPlan</code> contains exactly\n10713|<code>opens_existing_identity=true</code>,\n10714|<code>allow_blank_fallback=false</code>,\n10715|<code>bounded_continuation_turn_required:boolean</code>, and\n10716|<code>extensions</code>. <code>RollbackPlan</code> contains exactly\n10717|<code>required=true</code>, <code>retain_through=live_validated</code>,\n10718|<code>forbidden_after_provider_commit=true</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n10719|<code>ContractRequirement</code> contains exactly\n10720|<code>contract_id:string[1..256]</code> and <code>version:SemVer</code>.\n10721|\n10722|Clone Projected Object Manifest 1.0.0 contains exactly its schema/version,\n10723|<code>projected_object_manifest_id</code> under the omission rule,\n10724|<code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>projection_plan_id:digest</code>,\n10725|<code>target_environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>,\n10726|<code>expected_target_native_session_id:string[1..512]</code>,\n10727|<code>entries:ProjectedObjectEntry[0..65536]</code>,\n10728|<code>total_bytes:uint53</code>, and <code>extensions</code>. Entries are sorted\n10729|unique by operation sequence/resource key. <code>kind=blob</code> contains\n10730|exactly <code>operation_sequence</code>, <code>resource_key</code>,\n10731|<code>kind</code>, <code>mode:uint32[0..4095]|null</code>,\n10732|<code>byte_count:uint53</code>, <code>blob_id:digest</code>, and\n10733|<code>blob_descriptor_id:digest</code>. <code>kind=directory</code> contains\n10734|exactly sequence, key, kind, and mode. Entries partition Plan resources and\n10735|grant no live authority.\n10736|\n10737|Clone Read-Back Evidence Manifest 1.0.0 contains exactly its schema/version,\n10738|<code>read_back_evidence_manifest_id</code> under the omission rule,\n10739|<code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>mode:staged|live</code>,\n10740|<code>projection_plan_id:digest</code>,\n10741|<code>projected_object_manifest_id:digest</code>, equal expected and observed\n10742|native Session IDs, <code>observed_environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>,\n10743|<code>parsed_event_count:uint53</code>,\n10744|<code>parsed_head_ids:sorted unique string[1..512][0..1024]</code>,\n10745|<code>workspace_binding:WorkspaceBinding</code>,\n10746|<code>structural_digest:digest</code>,\n10747|<code>evidence_objects:EvidenceObject[0..65536]</code>, and\n10748|<code>extensions</code>. <code>EvidenceObject</code> contains exactly\n10749|<code>evidence_kind:native_sample|parser_trace|marker_observation</code>,\n10750|<code>media_type:string[1..128]</code>, <code>byte_count:uint53</code>,\n10751|<code>blob_id:digest</code>, and <code>blob_descriptor_id:digest</code>.\n10752|Evidence rows are sorted unique by evidence kind/blob ID. Staged and live\n10753|manifests are distinct and cannot be relabeled.\n10754|\n10755|Clone Validation Report 1.0.0 contains exactly\n10756|<code>schema=urn:ax:schema:clone-validation-report</code>,\n10757|<code>schema_version=1.0.0</code>,\n10758|<code>validation_report_id:digest</code> under the omission rule,\n10759|<code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>projection_plan_id:digest</code>,\n10760|<code>projected_object_manifest_id:digest</code>,\n10761|<code>staged_read_back_evidence_manifest_id:digest</code>,\n10762|<code>live_read_back_evidence_manifest_id:digest</code>,\n10763|<code>target_provider_manifest_id:digest</code>,\n10764|<code>fidelity_report_id:digest</code>,\n10765|<code>expected_target_native_session_id:string[1..512]</code>,\n10766|<code>observed_target_native_session_id:string[1..512]</code>,\n10767|<code>target_environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>,\n10768|<code>staged_structural_valid:boolean</code>,\n10769|<code>live_structural_valid:boolean</code>,\n10770|<code>semantic_marker_valid:boolean</code>,\n10771|<code>identity_valid:boolean</code>,\n10772|<code>workspace_binding_valid:boolean</code>,\n10773|<code>resume_surface_valid:boolean</code>,\n10774|<code>source_generation_revalidated:boolean</code>,\n10775|<code>findings:AdapterFinding[0..4096]</code>,\n10776|<code>valid:boolean</code>, and <code>extensions</code>. <code>valid=true</code>\n10777|requires every boolean true, matching native IDs/tuple, and no error finding.\n10778|\n10779|Migration Checkpoint 1.0.0 contains exactly\n10780|<code>schema=urn:ax:schema:migration-checkpoint</code>,\n10781|<code>schema_version=1.0.0</code>,\n10782|<code>migration_checkpoint_id:digest</code> under the omission rule,\n10783|<code>checkpoint_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>hop_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n10784|<code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>bundle_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n10785|<code>created_at:timestamp</code>, <code>source_snapshot_digest:digest</code>,\n10786|<code>source_checkpoint_id:digest|null</code>,\n10787|<code>canonical_session_id:digest</code>,\n10788|<code>projection_plan_id:digest</code>,\n10789|<code>source_environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>,\n10790|<code>source_native_session_id:string[1..512]</code>,\n10791|<code>source_logical_session_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n10792|<code>target_environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>,\n10793|<code>target_native_session_id:string[1..512]</code>,\n10794|<code>target_logical_session_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n10795|<code>previous_checkpoint_id:digest|null</code>,\n10796|<code>previous_lineage_receipt_id:digest|null</code>,\n10797|<code>projection_policy_digest:digest</code>,\n10798|<code>fidelity_basis_digest:digest</code>,\n10799|<code>report_locator:ReportLocator</code>,\n10800|<code>preserved_classes:sorted unique string[1..128][0..128]</code>,\n10801|<code>transformed_classes:sorted unique string[1..128][0..128]</code>,\n10802|<code>archived_classes:sorted unique string[1..128][0..128]</code>,\n10803|<code>unrecoverable_classes:sorted unique string[1..128][0..128]</code>,\n10804|<code>visible_projection:VisibleMigrationProjection</code>, and\n10805|<code>extensions</code>. <code>ReportLocator</code> contains exactly\n10806|<code>bundle_id:UUIDv7</code> and\n10807|<code>logical_path=reports/fidelity.json</code>; it is not a report digest.\n10808|<code>VisibleMigrationProjection</code> contains exactly\n10809|<code>authority=user_context</code>,\n10810|<code>target_event_ids:sorted unique digest[1..64]</code>,\n10811|<code>escaped_text:string[1..65536]</code>, and <code>extensions</code>. It is\n10812|never an assistant reply, system instruction, or authorization.\n10813|\n10814|Clone Lineage Receipt 1.0.0 contains exactly\n10815|<code>schema=urn:ax:schema:clone-lineage-receipt</code>,\n10816|<code>schema_version=1.0.0</code>,\n10817|<code>lineage_receipt_id:digest</code> under the omission rule,\n10818|<code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>bundle_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n10819|<code>source_kind:ax_session|external_native</code>,\n10820|<code>source_session_record_id:digest|null</code>,\n10821|<code>source_checkpoint_id:digest|null</code>,\n10822|<code>source_native_session_id:string[1..512]</code>,\n10823|<code>source_environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>,\n10824|<code>target_session_record_id:digest</code>,\n10825|<code>target_provider_identity_record_id:digest</code>,\n10826|<code>target_environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>,\n10827|<code>migration_checkpoint_id:digest</code>,\n10828|<code>projection_plan_id:digest</code>,\n10829|<code>validation_bundle_manifest_id:digest</code> naming G3,\n10830|<code>fidelity_report_id:digest</code>,\n10831|<code>validation_report_id:digest</code>,\n10832|<code>provider_committed_result_digest:digest</code>,\n10833|<code>target_checkpoint_id:digest</code>,\n10834|<code>clone_committed_event_id:digest</code>,\n10835|<code>previous_lineage_receipt_id:digest|null</code>,\n10836|<code>committed_at:timestamp</code>,\n10837|<code>operator_signature_blob_descriptor_id:digest|null</code>, and\n10838|<code>extensions</code>. AX-session source IDs are non-null exactly for that\n10839|source kind. The receipt never names G4, lease, approval, credential, task-board\n10840|goal, rollback token, or live authority.\n10841|\n10842|#### 13.14.3 Immutable bundle chain\n10843|\n10844|Clone Bundle Manifest 1.0.0 contains schema/version/omission-rule ID,\n10845|bundle/operation, generation, stage, immediate predecessor, tagged content,\n10846|operation-stable time, and extensions. Only these chains are legal:\n10847|\n10848|~~~text\n10849|G0 capture -> G1 canonical -> A2 archive (terminal)\n10850|G0 capture -> G1 canonical -> G2 projection -> G3 validation -> G4 committed\n10851|~~~\n10852|\n10853|G0 names Capture Manifest. G1 adds Canonical Session/Events. A2 adds archive\n10854|Fidelity Report and validation digest and forbids every target fact. G2 adds\n10855|Projection Plan, Migration Checkpoint, Projected Object Manifest, target\n10856|workspace Transfer Manifest, Materialization Plan 2, and staged evidence. G3\n10857|adds Provider prepared fact, target Provider Identity, ordinary live provider\n10858|Transfer Manifest, live evidence, and final reports. G4 adds Provider committed\n10859|fact, optional sole checkpoint-failure event, target Checkpoint,\n10860|<code>checkpoint.created</code>, <code>clone.committed</code>, and receipt.\n10861|\n10862|Stages cannot skip; operation/bundle remain constant; one predecessor cannot\n10863|have byte-different successors, including A2/G2. Identical replay returns the\n10864|existing ID. Rollback retains highest verified G0-G3, reports, and Journal.\n10865|Secure deletion is separate. Digest edges point only to lower layers or prior\n10866|hops. Migration uses a fidelity basis; Fidelity Report does not name Validation\n10867|Report; receipt names G3 and G4 names receipt; Checkpoint names only prior event\n10868|heads and announcing events point back. Digest cycles are forbidden.\n10869|\n10870|The complete Clone Bundle Manifest 1.0.0 common object contains exactly:\n10871|\n10872|| Member | Type and constraint |\n10873|| --- | --- |\n10874|| <code>schema</code> / <code>schema_version</code> | Exact <code>urn:ax:schema:session-clone-bundle</code> / <code>1.0.0</code> |\n10875|| <code>manifest_id</code> | JCS digest with only this member omitted |\n10876|| <code>bundle_id</code> / <code>operation_id</code> | UUIDv7 values constant across the selected branch |\n10877|| <code>generation</code> | uint53 in 0..4 |\n10878|| <code>stage</code> | <code>capture&#124;canonical&#124;archive&#124;projection&#124;validation&#124;committed</code> |\n10879|| <code>previous_manifest_id</code> | digest or null under the exact predecessor rule |\n10880|| <code>content</code> | Exactly one closed stage variant below; kind equals stage |\n10881|| <code>created_at</code> | Operation-stable diagnostic timestamp included in identity |\n10882|| <code>extensions</code> | Reverse-DNS keys; no normative references |\n10883|\n10884|The closed <code>content</code> union has exactly <code>kind</code> plus the\n10885|members in its row; members from every other row are forbidden:\n10886|\n10887|| Generation / kind | Exact additional members |\n10888|| --- | --- |\n10889|| G0 / <code>capture</code> | <code>capture_manifest_id:digest</code> |\n10890|| G1 / <code>canonical</code> | <code>canonical_session_id:digest</code>, <code>canonical_event_ids:digest[0..65536]</code> in Canonical Session order and unique |\n10891|| A2 / <code>archive</code> | <code>fidelity_report_id:digest</code>, <code>archive_validation_evidence_digest:digest</code>, <code>raw_complete:boolean</code>, <code>canonical_complete:boolean</code> |\n10892|| G2 / <code>projection</code> | <code>projection_plan_id:digest</code>, <code>migration_checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>projected_object_manifest_id:digest</code>, <code>target_workspace_manifest_id:digest</code>, <code>materialization_plan_id:digest</code>, <code>staged_read_back_evidence_manifest_id:digest</code> |\n10893|| G3 / <code>validation</code> | <code>provider_prepared_fact_digest:digest</code>, <code>target_provider_identity_record_id:digest</code>, <code>target_provider_manifest_id:digest</code>, <code>live_read_back_evidence_manifest_id:digest</code>, <code>fidelity_report_id:digest</code>, <code>validation_report_id:digest</code> |\n10894|| G4 / <code>committed</code> | <code>provider_committed_fact_digest:digest</code>, <code>checkpoint_failure_event_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>target_checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>checkpoint_created_event_id:digest</code>, <code>clone_committed_event_id:digest</code>, <code>lineage_receipt_id:digest</code> |\n10895|\n10896|G0 has null predecessor, G1 names G0, and generation 2 is exactly A2 naming G1\n10897|or G2 naming G1. A2 is terminal. The target branch continues G2 to G3 to G4,\n10898|each naming its immediate predecessor. A second byte-different successor of\n10899|any predecessor, including an A2/G2 fork, is an integrity failure; byte-identical\n10900|replay returns the existing identity. Provider prepared/committed fact digests\n10901|are sanitized terminal hashes, not object locators, and rollback tokens occur\n10902|only in Journal 3.\n10903|\n10904|#### 13.14.4 Transaction and target Checkpoint\n10905|\n10906|Materialization Plan 2.0.0 retains major-1 non-clone semantics but replaces\n10907|mandatory source checkpoint/lease fields with\n10908|<code>source_basis=ax_checkpoint|external_native</code> and adds\n10909|<code>intent=clone</code> plus Clone Projection. External basis contains\n10910|Capture Manifest, snapshot, generation, and tuple, never fabricated AX\n10911|ownership. Clone Projection binds all clone/projection/target identities.\n10912|Clone requires rollback, null prior checkpoint, collision absence, and\n10913|manifest/native-discovery/projection/read-back/resume-plan validations. Only a\n10914|clone Plan 2 may use Projected Object Manifest as provider merge input;\n10915|Transfer Manifest 1.0.0 remains unchanged.\n10916|\n10917|Materialization Plan 2.0.0 is a complete independently readable schema, not a\n10918|delta over Plan 1. Its closed top-level object contains exactly:\n10919|\n10920|| Field | Type and constraint |\n10921|| --- | --- |\n10922|| <code>schema</code> / <code>schema_version</code> | Exact Materialization Plan identifier / <code>2.0.0</code> |\n10923|| <code>plan_id</code> | JCS digest with only this member omitted |\n10924|| <code>kind</code> | <code>workspace&#124;provider&#124;task_board&#124;composite</code> |\n10925|| <code>intent</code> | Major-1 intents plus <code>clone</code> |\n10926|| <code>subject_id</code> | UUIDv7 target Session for clone |\n10927|| <code>source_basis</code> | Closed Materialization Source Basis below |\n10928|| <code>source_manifest_ids</code> | Sorted unique digest[0..1024] pre-existing inputs |\n10929|| <code>derived_manifest_ids</code> | Sorted unique digest[0..1024] fork outputs or clone projection outputs |\n10930|| <code>fork_projection</code> | Existing closed Fork Workspace Projection or null; non-null exactly for fork |\n10931|| <code>clone_projection</code> | Closed Clone Projection or null; non-null exactly for clone |\n10932|| <code>prepared_for_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 executing allowlisted host |\n10933|| <code>authorities</code> | Existing closed <code>RootAuthority[0..512]</code> |\n10934|| <code>expected_prior_checkpoint_id</code> | digest or null; null for fresh clone target |\n10935|| <code>operations</code> | Existing closed <code>PlanOperation[0..65536]</code> with major-1 ordering/path rules |\n10936|| <code>exclusions</code> | Sorted unique exclusion-class[0..128] |\n10937|| <code>validations</code> | Sorted unique validation-name[1..9] |\n10938|| <code>commit_strategy</code> | Existing major-1 enum |\n10939|| <code>rollback_required</code> | boolean; true for clone |\n10940|| <code>created_by_host_id</code> / <code>created_at</code> | UUIDv7 / diagnostic timestamp |\n10941|| <code>extensions</code> | Reverse-DNS keys only |\n10942|\n10943|Materialization Source Basis is a closed union. <code>kind=ax_checkpoint</code>\n10944|contains exactly <code>kind</code>, <code>source_checkpoint_id:digest</code>,\n10945|<code>source_lease_epoch:uint53&gt;0</code>, and\n10946|<code>source_lease_id:UUIDv4</code>. <code>kind=external_native</code> contains\n10947|exactly <code>kind</code>, <code>capture_manifest_id:digest</code>,\n10948|<code>source_snapshot_digest:digest</code>,\n10949|<code>source_store_generation:string[1..512]</code>, and\n10950|<code>source_environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>. Every non-clone intent\n10951|requires AX checkpoint basis. External-native basis never fabricates an AX\n10952|checkpoint or lease.\n10953|\n10954|Clone Projection contains exactly\n10955|<code>projection_version=session_clone_v1</code>,\n10956|<code>clone_operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>bundle_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n10957|<code>capture_manifest_id:digest</code>,\n10958|<code>canonical_session_id:digest</code>,\n10959|<code>projection_plan_id:digest</code>,\n10960|<code>migration_checkpoint_id:digest</code>,\n10961|<code>projected_object_manifest_id:digest</code>,\n10962|<code>target_workspace_manifest_id:digest</code>,\n10963|<code>target_session_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n10964|<code>target_provider_id:provider-id</code>,\n10965|<code>expected_target_native_session_id:string[1..512]</code>,\n10966|<code>target_environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>, and\n10967|<code>extensions</code>. Clone requires null fork projection,\n10968|<code>kind=provider|composite</code>, a direct target Session Record whose\n10969|identities equal these fields, null prior checkpoint, and collision absence.\n10970|\n10971|For clone, <code>derived_manifest_ids</code> contains exactly the Clone\n10972|Projected Object Manifest plus target-specific workspace Transfer Manifests;\n10973|source manifests are pre-existing validated workspace inputs. Only clone\n10974|permits <code>merge_provider_store.input_id</code> to name the projected-object\n10975|manifest. Its entries form a disjoint complete partition by Plan operation\n10976|sequence beneath prevalidated authorities. Non-clone Plan 2 retains the Plan 1\n10977|rule that install/merge inputs are Transfer Manifests or Task-board Bundles.\n10978|\n10979|The complete validation-name registry is the six major-1 names\n10980|<code>backend_identity</code>, <code>manifest_closure</code>,\n10981|<code>provider_native_discovery</code>, <code>task_board_bundle</code>,\n10982|<code>task_board_validate</code>, and <code>workspace_state</code>, plus\n10983|<code>clone_projection</code>, <code>target_native_read_back</code>, and\n10984|<code>target_resume_plan</code>. Every clone requires manifest closure,\n10985|provider discovery, and all three clone validations; composite clone also\n10986|requires workspace state. No non-clone plan carries a clone validation.\n10987|\n10988|~~~text\n10989|resolving -> snapshotting -> captured -> normalized -> planned\n10990|-> preparing -> prepared -> publishing -> published\n10991|-> live_validating -> finalizing -> provider_committed\n10992|-> sealing_checkpoint -> committed -> lineage_published\n10993|archive: normalized -> archive_validating -> archived\n10994|rollback before provider commit: publishing|published|live_validating|finalizing\n10995|-> rolling_back -> rolled_back\n10996|~~~\n10997|\n10998|Journal 3.0.0 is clone-only and closed. It cumulatively fixes\n10999|materialization/phase/source basis, Plan and transfer state, authorities/chunks,\n11000|existing Provider Journal Transaction, both execution bindings, G0-G4 IDs,\n11001|source checks, target identity/tuple, evidence/reports/manifests, caller-stable\n11002|Provider request/result facts, deterministic Checkpoint time/head/event suffix,\n11003|receipt, errors, and times. Fields become non-null only at their phase and then\n11004|remain immutable. Rollback token stays only in Provider Journal Transaction.\n11005|A failed journal read is integrity failure, never absence.\n11006|\n11007|Materialization Journal 3.0.0 is a complete clone-only schema and does not\n11008|inherit Journal 2. The closed top-level object contains exactly:\n11009|\n11010|| Field | Type and constraint |\n11011|| --- | --- |\n11012|| <code>schema</code> / <code>schema_version</code> / <code>document_kind</code> | Exact Journal identifier / <code>3.0.0</code> / <code>journal</code> |\n11013|| <code>materialization_id</code> | UUIDv7 allocated with the operation before first journal write |\n11014|| <code>phase</code> | <code>snapshotting&#124;captured&#124;normalized&#124;planned&#124;preparing&#124;prepared&#124;publishing&#124;published&#124;live_validating&#124;finalizing&#124;provider_committed&#124;sealing_checkpoint&#124;committed&#124;lineage_published&#124;rolling_back&#124;rolled_back&#124;failed</code> |\n11015|| <code>source_basis</code> | Closed Journal Source Basis below, immutable |\n11016|| <code>plan_id</code> | digest or null; null before G2 then immutable Plan 2 ID |\n11017|| <code>transfer_id</code> | UUIDv7 or null; non-null only when projected inputs use AX object transfer |\n11018|| <code>managed_replica_id</code> | UUIDv7 or null; non-null exactly when target workspace bytes participate |\n11019|| <code>authority_states</code> | map(root-id, existing Authority Journal State)[0..512] |\n11020|| <code>expected_prior_checkpoint_id</code> | Always null for clone |\n11021|| <code>completed_blob_chunks</code> / <code>verified_blob_ids</code> | Existing Journal-2 keyed chunk map / verified whole-blob set |\n11022|| <code>provider_transaction</code> | Existing closed Provider Journal Transaction or null |\n11023|| <code>task_board_transaction</code> | Always null in v0.3 clone |\n11024|| <code>destination_marker_id</code> | digest or null; only composite clone with workspace materialization |\n11025|| <code>clone</code> | Required closed Clone Journal State below |\n11026|| <code>last_error</code> | Redacted Structured Error 1.1 or null |\n11027|| <code>started_at</code> / <code>updated_at</code> | Diagnostic timestamps |\n11028|| <code>extensions</code> | Reverse-DNS machine-local keys only |\n11029|\n11030|Journal Source Basis is a closed union. <code>kind=ax_session</code> contains\n11031|exactly <code>kind</code>, <code>source_session_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n11032|<code>source_session_record_id:digest</code>,\n11033|<code>source_checkpoint_id:digest</code>,\n11034|<code>source_lease_epoch:uint53&gt;0</code>,\n11035|<code>source_lease_id:UUIDv4</code>, and\n11036|<code>source_environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>.\n11037|<code>kind=external_native</code> contains exactly <code>kind</code>,\n11038|<code>source_native_session_id:string[1..512]</code>,\n11039|<code>source_environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>, and\n11040|<code>inspected_store_generation:string[1..512]</code>.\n11041|\n11042|Clone Journal State contains exactly the following members. Every nullable\n11043|member is present with null until admitted by the phase matrix:\n11044|\n11045|| Member | Type |\n11046|| --- | --- |\n11047|| <code>clone_operation_id</code> / <code>bundle_id</code> | UUIDv7, immutable |\n11048|| <code>session_adapter_bindings</code> | Exactly two <code>SessionAdapterExecutionBinding</code> values ordered source then target, immutable |\n11049|| <code>current_bundle_manifest_id</code>, <code>capture_manifest_id</code>, <code>canonical_session_id</code>, <code>projection_plan_id</code>, <code>migration_checkpoint_id</code>, <code>target_projected_object_manifest_id</code> | digest or null |\n11050|| <code>source_snapshot_digest</code> | digest or null |\n11051|| <code>source_store_generation</code> | string[1..512] or null |\n11052|| <code>prepublication_source_check_id</code> / <code>postpublication_source_check_id</code> | digest or null |\n11053|| <code>expected_target_native_session_id</code> | string[1..512] or null |\n11054|| <code>target_environment</code> | EnvironmentTuple or null |\n11055|| <code>staged_read_back_evidence_manifest_id</code>, <code>live_read_back_evidence_manifest_id</code>, <code>fidelity_report_id</code>, <code>validation_report_id</code> | digest or null |\n11056|| <code>target_workspace_manifest_id</code>, <code>target_provider_identity_record_id</code>, <code>target_provider_manifest_id</code> | digest or null |\n11057|| <code>provider_operation_id</code> | UUIDv7 or null; caller-stable Provider materialize operation |\n11058|| <code>provider_materialize_request_digest</code> | digest or null; exact canonical Provider request body |\n11059|| <code>provider_prepared_result_digest</code>, <code>provider_committed_result_digest</code>, <code>provider_rolled_back_result_digest</code> | digest or null; sanitized result facts |\n11060|| <code>target_checkpoint_created_at</code> | timestamp or null; caller-stable suffix input |\n11061|| <code>checkpoint_failure_event_id</code> | digest or null; at most one |\n11062|| <code>target_checkpoint_event_heads</code> | sorted unique digest[1..64] or null; fixed once |\n11063|| <code>target_checkpoint_id</code>, <code>checkpoint_created_event_id</code>, <code>clone_committed_event_id</code>, <code>lineage_receipt_id</code> | digest or null |\n11064|| <code>extensions</code> | Reverse-DNS machine-local keys only |\n11065|\n11066|The journal is first written at <code>snapshotting</code> after read-only\n11067|resolve/manifest/probe/inspect fix both bindings and source basis, but before\n11068|snapshot proof or capture. <code>resolving</code> has no Journal 3 and no\n11069|mutation. The required/non-null matrix is cumulative; facts introduced in a\n11070|row remain immutable thereafter, unadmitted nullable fields remain null, and\n11071|maps/sets remain empty:\n11072|\n11073|| First phase | Newly required durable facts |\n11074|| --- | --- |\n11075|| <code>snapshotting</code> | Operation/bundle/materialization IDs, two bindings, source basis; every object/result/plan field null |\n11076|| <code>captured</code> | Source snapshot digest/generation, Capture Manifest, current G0 |\n11077|| <code>normalized</code> | Canonical Session, current G1 |\n11078|| <code>planned</code> | Projection Plan, Migration Checkpoint, planned target identity/environment, accepted policy; current manifest remains G1 |\n11079|| <code>preparing</code> | Isolated target sink may exist; Plan, authorities, Provider transaction remain null/empty |\n11080|| <code>prepared</code> | Projected Object Manifest, any target workspace Transfer Manifest, staged evidence, Plan 2, exact authorities, current G2; target Provider Identity/Transfer Manifest absent; target Session Record/lease/event creation follows this durable phase |\n11081|| <code>publishing</code> | Provider operation ID, byte-identical request digest, Provider transaction <code>unknown</code> with exact authority, prepublication source-check ID |\n11082|| <code>published</code> | Provider <code>prepared</code>, non-null rollback token and prepared-result digest, exact discovered target Provider Identity, postpublication source-check ID |\n11083|| <code>live_validating</code> | Same retained Provider state/token; live evidence and unchanged Provider capture may accumulate |\n11084|| <code>finalizing</code> | Live evidence, ordinary target provider Transfer Manifest, Fidelity/Validation Reports, current G3, fixed target manifests/checkpoint creation time; Provider remains rollback-capable |\n11085|| <code>provider_committed</code> | Provider <code>committed</code>, null rollback token, committed-result digest; prepared digest retained |\n11086|| <code>sealing_checkpoint</code> | Same committed facts; optional sole failure event, then fixed heads and deterministic checkpoint/event suffix IDs in durable prefix order |\n11087|| <code>committed</code> | Target Checkpoint, <code>checkpoint.created</code>, and <code>clone.committed</code> IDs non-null; receipt null |\n11088|| <code>lineage_published</code> | Lineage Receipt and current G4 non-null |\n11089|| <code>rolling_back</code> | Provider <code>unknown&#124;prepared</code>; rollback intent durable; committed-result digest null |\n11090|| <code>rolled_back</code> | Provider <code>rolled_back</code>, null token, rolled-back-result digest non-null, committed digest null; highest G0-G3 retained |\n11091|| <code>failed</code> | <code>last_error</code> non-null; every previously durable identity/effect unchanged |\n11092|\n11093|The existing Provider Journal Transaction is the sole custody location for\n11094|Provider transaction ID, transaction authority, state, rollback token, and\n11095|last status time. Its operation/materialization/provider/transaction/plan IDs\n11096|equal Journal 3 and Plan 2. The token is forbidden from Clone Journal State,\n11097|bundle, report, receipt, event, log, or replicated object. Prepared-result\n11098|evidence may coexist with exactly one of committed-result or rolled-back-result\n11099|evidence; committed and rolled-back digests are mutually exclusive. Every\n11100|phase and Provider-state change is persisted before the next external effect.\n11101|\n11102|Prepare writes isolated bytes and validates staged read-back. Core rechecks\n11103|source generation and target collision before unchanged Provider\n11104|<code>materialize</code>. Provider <code>prepared</code> maps to outer\n11105|published while rollback remains. Core rechecks source, independently reads\n11106|the inert live target, and captures an ordinary provider Transfer Manifest.\n11107|Finalize persists intent before unchanged Provider commit with dormant validated\n11108|activation. Provider committed discards rollback state. Ambiguous responses\n11109|first reconcile status against the same authority. Unknown is parked, never\n11110|absence. Pre-commit failures discard sinks or explicitly roll back while\n11111|retaining evidence. Post-commit rollback is forbidden; recovery completes the\n11112|same deterministic suffix or remains input-blocked, never allocating another\n11113|target, lease, transaction, or process.\n11114|\n11115|After Provider commit, core seals one ordinary validated Checkpoint 1.0.0 for\n11116|the new Session/epoch-1 lease. It names exact workspace and ordinary live\n11117|provider Transfer Manifests and proves the exact native identity, input blocked,\n11118|full idle, zero processes and handles. It names pre-checkpoint event heads,\n11119|then core emits <code>checkpoint.created</code> and\n11120|<code>clone.committed</code>. A definitive semantic failure before head\n11121|fixation emits at most one <code>clone.failed(phase=checkpoint)</code>; storage\n11122|crashes retry without a failure event. Recovery uses the existing failure head\n11123|and never a replacement Checkpoint.\n11124|\n11125|After any ambiguous Provider call, core first invokes unchanged\n11126|<code>materialize-status</code> with the caller-known transaction authority.\n11127|The lost-response mapping is closed:\n11128|\n11129|| Ambiguous outer boundary | Provider status | Required action |\n11130|| --- | --- | --- |\n11131|| <code>publishing</code>, lost materialize response | <code>prepared</code> | Persist recovered token/prepared facts once; continue at <code>published</code> |\n11132|| Same | <code>unknown</code> | <code>recoverable_parked_state</code>; no new target or transaction |\n11133|| Same | <code>rolled_back</code> | Record <code>rolled_back</code>; retain G0-G2 |\n11134|| Same | <code>committed</code> | Integrity-park because commit intent was not durable; do not invent success or byte rollback |\n11135|| <code>published&#124;live_validating</code> | <code>prepared</code> | Resume the same postpublication validation or roll back with the same authority |\n11136|| Same | <code>unknown</code> | Park input-blocked |\n11137|| Same | <code>committed&#124;rolled_back</code> | Reconcile only with matching already-durable terminal intent/result; otherwise integrity-park |\n11138|| <code>finalizing</code>, lost commit response | <code>prepared</code> | Safe-retry byte-identical <code>materialize-commit</code> |\n11139|| Same | <code>committed</code> | Persist facts and the deterministic Checkpoint/event/lineage suffix |\n11140|| Same | <code>unknown</code> | Park; never reopen with a fresh identity |\n11141|| Same | <code>rolled_back</code> | Integrity-park unless matching earlier rollback intent is durable |\n11142|| <code>rolling_back</code>, lost rollback response | <code>prepared</code> | Safe-retry byte-identical rollback |\n11143|| Same | <code>rolled_back</code> | Persist outer rolled-back facts |\n11144|| Same | <code>committed</code> | Byte rollback forbidden; park the exact input-blocked target |\n11145|| Same | <code>unknown</code> | <code>recoverable_parked_state</code> |\n11146|| <code>provider_committed&#124;sealing_checkpoint</code>, restart | <code>committed</code> | Revalidate exact closed target and persist only the missing deterministic suffix |\n11147|\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
