{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4d1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ceca-cad7-7401-b120-5d187a59f4b1"},"sequence":195,"recorded_at":1780531400000385,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f679b6f1-9902-47f8-8dc1-d6bbf0923c83","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"f679b6f1-9902-47f8-8dc1-d6bbf0923c83","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f679b6f1-9902-47f8-8dc1-d6bbf0923c83"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0cecb-3598-7b32-986d-34caa077733f"},"task_id":"01a0cecb-3598-7b32-986d-34caa077733f","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0cecb-3598-7b32-986d-34caa077733f","chunk":"Read text file `internal/cloneproject/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n1|# Projection Fidelity Clause Coverage (TASK-260830-32ypr2)\n2|\n3|Owner: `internal/cloneproject`. Authority:\n4|`internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`, Sections 7.8, 10.2, 13.14.1\n5|(the pinned sections are byte-identical to v0.6.0).\n6|This is the FINAL leaf's clause record for the projection-fidelity\n7|closure; the `internal/traceability` registry bindings and re-pin\n8|ship in this leaf as well (see the Story-close section below).\n9|\n10|## Why this package normalizes instead of clonebundle or clonesnap\n11|\n12|The first leaf (`internal/clonebundle`) owns the capture contracts:\n13|the closed manifest/boundary/session/event shapes, their builders\n14|and decoders. The second leaf (`internal/clonesnap`) owns the\n15|capture OPERATION over a real provider store. This package owns\n16|NORMALIZATION: deriving Canonical Sessions and Canonical Events\n17|from captured bytes. Every event and the session seal through the\n18|landed `clonebundle` builders (`BuildCanonicalEvent`,\n19|`BuildCanonicalSession`, `CheckOrdinalContiguity`,\n20|`RefuseUnstableForTarget`, `InstallRawBlob`) and re-decode through\n21|the landed decoders before return; overflow Blob Descriptors seal\n22|through `clonesnap.BuildBlobDescriptor`; no second manifest,\n23|session, event, blob, or identity model exists here.\n24|\n25|## Landed-owner reuse\n26|\n27|| Scope | Owner | Use |\n28||---|---|---|\n29|| Session/event/evidence shapes | `internal/clonebundle` | all Build/Decode/Check/Refuse entries above |\n30|| Overflow descriptor shape | `internal/clonesnap` | `BuildBlobDescriptor` (errors wrapped with the overflow cause) |\n31|| Blob install (no-replace, fsync, verify) | `internal/clonebundle` + `internal/localstore` | `InstallRawBlob`, `ObjectStore.PutBlob` |\n32|| Digests, UUIDv7, timestamps | `internal/scalar` | `ParseDigest`, `SHA256Digest`, `ParseUUIDv7` |\n33|| Character string measure | `internal/environ` | `StringLength` at every native bound |\n34|| Strict JSON framing | `internal/environ` | `DecodeStrictObject` at `strictMembers`: both frame sites (record envelope, per-kind bodies) refuse lone-surrogate escapes, duplicate members, and trailing data before any member is read; the envelope is then read from the admitted map by exact member name with no second decoder, so case-folded aliases are inert extras (pinned by `TestNormalizeCaseAliasEnvelopeIgnoresUnclaimedMembers`) |\n35|| uint53 value gate | `internal/environ` | `CheckUint53Bounds` at `bodyUint53` and the envelope version check: fractions, exponents, strings, and out-of-range magnitudes refuse as not-a-uint53 |\n36|| Canonical bytes | `internal/canonicaljson` | `Canonicalize`, `CalculateObjectIdentity` (tests resolve overflow descriptors) |\n37|\n38|## Fixture-native per-kind payload fact registry\n39|\n40|Section 13.14.1 requires payloads to carry only their registered\n41|typed facts. The envelope and value model are landed (`checkPayload`\n42|in `clonebundle`); this package registers the exact facts it emits\n43|for each kind it projects. No other Canonical kind is emitted here.\n44|\n45|| Kind | Exact facts |\n46||---|---|\n47|| `user_message`, `assistant_message`, `reasoning_summary` | `content_blocks` (one `text` block, inline at or under 64 KiB, else `blob_descriptor_id` + `media_type`), `extensions` |\n48|| `opaque_reasoning` | `protection` (`encrypted`\\|`signed`), `byte_count`, `blob_descriptor_id`, `extensions` |\n49|| `opaque_event` (unknown record) | `native_type`, `byte_count`, `blob_descriptor_id`, `extensions` |\n50|| `opaque_event` (protected known record) | `native_type`, `protection`, `byte_count`, `blob_descriptor_id`, `extensions` |\n51|| `opaque_event` (unknown member) | `native_item_key`, `byte_count`, `blob_descriptor_id`, `extensions` |\n52|| `instruction_snapshot` | `authority` (`low` forced for foreign), `directives`, `extensions` |\n53|| `tool_definition_snapshot` | `tool_name`, `definition_digest`, `callable` (always false), `extensions` |\n54|| `tool_call` | `call_id`, `tool_name`, `resolution` (`completed`\\|`aborted`), `extensions` |\n55|| `tool_result` | `call_id`, `status` (`ok`\\|`error`), `resolution`, `extensions` |\n56|| `usage` | `input_tokens`, `output_tokens`, `extensions` |\n57|\n58|## Clause map\n59|\n60|| Pinned clause | Production entry | Test |\n61||---|---|---|\n62|| 13.14.1 unknown native records become raw-addressable opaque events | `Normalize`, `dispatchRecord` | `TestNormalizeUnknownRecordBecomesOpaqueEvent` (kind, `opaque` visibility, `unknown_native_event` reason, raw range resolves to the exact line); `TestNormalizeMultiRecordRefsResolveAtAssertedOffsets` (every event's `RawRefs[0]` resolves to its own line with offsets `0`, `len(l1)+1`, `len(l1)+len(l2)+2` asserted, multibyte first line); `TestNormalizeUnterminatedTailResolvesWithOffset` (a multi-line member without a trailing newline keeps its last record with its offset asserted); `TestNormalizeCRLFResolvesWithCarriageReturn` (each CRLF range covers its line plus the CR and resolves exactly) |\n63|| 13.14.1 almost-known records are never coerced into a neighbouring kind | `dispatchRecord` (exact type switch) | `TestNormalizeAlmostKnownRecordBecomesOpaqueEvent` (`message/smoke` stays `opaque_event`, never `user_message`) |\n64|| 13.14.1 unknown-class members become whole-member opaque events | `collectMembers` | `TestNormalizeUnknownMemberBecomesWholeMemberOpaque` (offset 0, full length, null native IDs, resolves to the whole member) |\n65|| 13.14.1 opaque events are never dropped, guessed, or re-typed | `Normalize` (deterministic order), `parseNativeLine` (strict-map envelope) | `TestNormalizeOpaqueIsStableAcrossProjections` (project twice, byte-identical, still `opaque_event`); `TestNormalizeCaseAliasEnvelopeIgnoresUnclaimedMembers/kind_alias_after` + `/kind_alias_before` (a `NATIVE_TYPE` alias in either document order still projects `opaque_event`, never coerced into a neighbouring kind) |\n66|| 13.14.1 foreign encrypted reasoning is opaque-preserved | `dispatchProtected` | `TestNormalizeForeignEncryptedReasoningStaysOpaque` (`opaque_reasoning`, `foreign_encrypted_payload`, no content members, byte-exact round trip) |\n67|| 13.14.1 foreign signed reasoning is opaque-preserved | `dispatchProtected` | `TestNormalizeForeignSignedReasoningStaysOpaque` (`foreign_signature_unverifiable`, byte-exact) |\n68|| 13.14.1 native protected reasoning stays opaque with no foreign code | `dispatchProtected`, `cryptoReasons` | `TestNormalizeNativeProtectedReasoningStaysOpaque` (empty reasons) |\n69|| 13.14.1 protected known content never reaches a semantic kind | `dispatchProtected` | `TestNormalizeProtectedMessageBecomesOpaqueEvent` (encrypted assistant message is `opaque_event`) |\n70|| 13.14.1 unknown+protected records carry both stable reasons | `dispatchProtected` | `TestNormalizeUnknownProtectedRecordCarriesBothReasons` |\n71|| 13.14.1 foreign instructions are low-authority history | `dispatchInstruction`, `foldInstructions` | `TestNormalizeForeignInstructionCannotChangeEffectiveSnapshot` (effective snapshot native-only, foreign payload pins `low`), `TestNormalizeForeignOnlyInstructionLeavesSnapshotEmpty`, `TestNormalizeCaseAliasEnvelopeIgnoresUnclaimedMembers/origin_alias` (an `Origin` alias cannot promote foreign history into the snapshot) |\n72|| 13.14.1 foreign encrypted reasoning is never promoted by an alias | `parseNativeLine` (strict-map envelope), `dispatchProtected` | `TestNormalizeCaseAliasEnvelopeIgnoresUnclaimedMembers/protection_alias` (a `Protection` alias cannot downgrade the record: the plaintext body refuses) |\n73|| 13.14.1 attribution follows the claimed actor member, never an alias | `parseNativeLine` (strict-map envelope), `checkActors` | `TestNormalizeCaseAliasEnvelopeIgnoresUnclaimedMembers/actor_alias` (an `Actor` alias cannot re-attribute an unmapped subagent record to `main`) |\n74|| 13.14.1 unprotected reasoning summaries project internal | `dispatchMessage` (default arm) | `TestNormalizeReasoningSummaryProjectsInternal` (kind `reasoning_summary`, `internal`, content block, `exact`) |\n75|| 13.14.1 every emitted kind stamps capture status exact | `evidenceFor` | `TestNormalizeCaptureStatusExactForEveryKind` (one record per kind, every event asserts `exact`) |\n76|| 13.14.1 the native instruction fold is last-wins | `foldInstructions` | `TestNormalizeLastNativeInstructionWins` (two native records, the snapshot carries the second) |\n77|| 13.14.1 the external selector seals as an external actor | `buildResult` | `TestNormalizeExternalActorSealsAsExternal` (kind `external`, parented on `main`) |\n78|| 13.14.1 source usage is not target accounting | `foldUsage` | `TestNormalizeSourceUsageIsNotTargetAccounting` (source sums exact, target zero) |\n79|| 13.14.1 historical tools are inert; call+result resolves completed | `resolveToolCalls`, `deriveLiveSurface` | `TestNormalizeToolMatrix/call_with_result` (kinds, `internal` visibility, `completed`, empty live surface) |\n80|| 13.14.1 incomplete calls become aborted history and block pending action | `resolveToolCalls`, `deriveLiveSurface` | `TestNormalizeToolMatrix/call_without_result` (`aborted`, `unsafe_pending_action`, empty live surface), `TestNormalizeToolMatrix/result_without_call` (orphan `aborted`) |\n81|| 13.14.1 results arriving after the boundary complete the same call | `resolveToolCalls` over two captures | `TestNormalizeResultAfterBoundaryCompletes` (first capture `aborted`, second `completed`) |\n82|| 13.14.1 nested calls attribute to a parented subagent actor | `checkActors`, `buildResult` | `TestNormalizeToolMatrix/nested_subagent_call` (subagent actor, parent is main) |\n83|| 13.14.1 definitions never register a callable tool | `deriveLiveSurface`, `dispatchDefinition` | `TestNormalizeToolDefinitionNeverRegistersCallable` (`callable` false, `CallableTools` empty) |\n84|| 13.14.1 live surface stays empty over mixed history | `deriveLiveSurface` | `TestNormalizeLiveSurfaceStaysEmpty` |\n85|| 13.14.1 Canonical Session bounds (actors, ordered event IDs, head) | `buildResult` | `TestNormalizeSealsSessionShape` (ordinals, parent chain, head is last) |\n86|| 13.14.1 message-like inline content at most 64 KiB; oversized becomes a blob reference | `contentBlockForText`, `installOverflow` | `TestNormalizeInlineContentBoundary` (65536 inline, 65537 blob-referenced and byte-exact, never truncated) |\n87|| 13.14.1 same captured bytes project byte-identical output | `Normalize` (sorted inputs, no clock), `buildResult` actor sort | `TestNormalizeIsDeterministic`, `TestNormalizeActorOrderIsDeterministic` (three extra actors, twelve projections, one distinct session) |\n88|| 13.14.1 unstable_archive cannot enter target projection | `Normalize` via `RefuseUnstableForTarget` | `TestNormalizeRefusesUnstableCapture` |\n89|| 13.14.1 capture closure: manifest link, blob fetch, digest/size agreement | `Normalize`, `collectMembers` | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/manifest_closure_drift/tampered_blob/missing_blob/blob_size_drift` (each arm asserts its own message) |\n90|| 13.14.1 framing-malformed records refuse with member+line named | `strictMembers`, `splitRecordLines`, `parseNativeLine`, body decoders | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/malformed_json_line/missing_envelope_member/bad_envelope_version/string_envelope_version/blank_line/unknown_body_member/call_live_followup_member/result_live_attestation_member/body_text_number/body_live_attestation_string/body_missing_text/empty_directive/contradictory_protection/protected_plaintext_body/unknown_protected_plaintext_body/unknown_type_without_body/lone_surrogate_text/lone_surrogate_envelope/duplicate_envelope_member/duplicate_body_member/trailing_bytes/invalid_utf8_line/empty_subagent_name` |\n91|| 13.14.1 live claims by captured history refuse | `deriveLiveSurface`, `resolveToolCalls` | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/live_attestation_claim/live_followup_claim` |\n92|| 13.14.1 ambiguous tool pairings refuse | `resolveToolCalls` | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/duplicate_call_id/duplicate_result_id` |\n93|| 13.14.1 exact actor mapping (referenced iff mapped) | `checkActors` | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/unmapped_actor/unmapped_extra_actor/main_actor_in_map` |\n94|| 13.14.1 instruction authority, usage value model, and result status vocabulary | `decodeInstructionBody`, `bodyUint53`, `decodeToolResultBody` | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/bad_instruction_authority/fractional_usage/unsafe_usage_magnitude/string_usage_number/bad_result_status` |\n95|| 13.14.1 reasoning type/protection agreement refuses per arm | `dispatchProtected` | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/encrypted_type_signed_protection/signed_type_encrypted_protection` |\n96|| 13.14.1 protected non-reasoning tool records reach opaque only via the fold-skip | `foldTools` skip, `dispatchProtected` | `TestNormalizeProtectedToolCallStaysOpaqueHistory` (protected call is `opaque_event`, the unprotected result an aborted orphan, live surface empty) |\n97|| 13.14.1 non-JSONL included members refuse the whole projection | `collectMembers` JSONL parsing | `TestNormalizeNonJSONLIncludedMemberRefuses` (stated bound: routing by member class is sibling scope) |\n98|| 10.2 Blob Descriptor reference resolves to installed bytes | `installOverflow` | `TestNormalizeInlineContentBoundary` (`mustResolveOverflow` through the sink) |\n99|| 10.2 fsync + verify + atomic install before referencing | `InstallRawBlob`, `PutBlob` (landed) | `TestNormalizeIsIdempotentIntoSharedSink` (replay verifies and reuses, blob count stable) |\n100|| 7.8 large data by reference, never embedded in the 8 MiB frame | `sessadapter.DecodeRequestFrame` (`MaxFrameBytes`) | `TestDecodeRequestFrameRefusesOversizeFrame`, `TestFrameBoundEdges` (sessadapter owner; `session-adapter-frame-bound` case). `TestNormalizeInlineContentBoundary` proves reference-not-embedded at the content level but constructs no frame and discharges no 7.8 clause |\n101|| 1.6 string measure in characters | `environ.StringLength` at every native bound | `TestNormalizeMultibyteStringMeasure` (512-char ID admits, 513 refuses) and `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/long_subagent_name`; per-edge directive/call/tool-name rows are stated bounds |\n102|| 1.6 text is valid UTF-8, never rewritten | `environ.DecodeStrictObject` at `strictMembers` (both frame sites) after line-level `utf8.Valid`; envelope values come from the strict map by exact name | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/lone_surrogate_text/lone_surrogate_envelope/duplicate_envelope_member/duplicate_body_member/trailing_bytes/invalid_utf8_line`; `TestNormalizeCaseAliasEnvelopeIgnoresUnclaimedMembers/body_alias` (sealed content ignores the `Body` alias) + `/evidence_alias` (the evidence identity ignores the `Native_Event_Id` alias) |\n103|\n104|## Durability\n105|\n106|This package holds no local state. Its only durable write is\n107|overflow-blob installation: payload bytes through the landed\n108|`InstallRawBlob` (descriptor identity plus blob-ID/size agreement)\n109|and descriptor bytes through `ObjectStore.PutBlob`, both\n110|content-addressed under the landed no-replace discipline (stage,\n111|fsync, verify, atomic install). Crash semantics are the landed\n112|`localstore` discipline's (proven by that package's fault suites);\n113|this package adds bundle atomicity at the return:\n114|`TestNormalizeFailureReturnsNoPartialBundle` proves a mid-projection\n115|fetch failure returns no partial bundle and a healthy re-run\n116|converges, and `TestNormalizeIsIdempotentIntoSharedSink` proves a\n117|replay into a shared sink seals byte-identical output while the sink\n118|blob count stays stable (verify-and-reuse, no reinstall). A refused\n119|projection may leave orphan overflow blobs from earlier units in the\n120|sink; they are content-addressed and inert, and no bundle ever\n121|references them.\n122|\n123|## Mutants\n124|\n125|`testdata/mutant_harness.py` ships 80 narrowing rows, 5 labelled\n126|non-narrowing rows, and the harmless `C-doc-comment` SURVIVED\n127|control. Every narrowing weakens one gate to admit exactly one\n128|member of the class it must reject, and every killer drives the\n129|production `Normalize` entry over real captured bytes.\n130|`N-native-type-token` and `N-protection-encrypted` are the\n131|token-preserving attacks: the searched-for text still matches\n132|while the decision changes, and the killers execute the\n133|behavioral suite. The six `N-alias-*` rows restore the\n134|case-folded read for exactly one envelope member each; every\n135|other alias stays an unclaimed extra under the plant.\n136|`N-empty-projection` is labelled single-member class,\n137|`N-overflow-truncate` is labelled behaviour swap,\n138|`N-pending-aborted` is labelled add-arm (`Normalize` passes nil\n139|live work orders, so the narrowed condition alone cannot pend\n140|from the entry and the plant appends the call explicitly), and\n141|`N-offset-newline` is labelled behaviour swap (drops the newline\n142|stride from the offset accumulation; the asserted offsets\n143|redden), and `N-unterminated-tail-drop` is labelled behaviour\n144|drop (drops the unterminated last line of a multi-line member;\n145|the missing tail event reddens); no other row is an arm-delete. The five `N-strict-*`\n146|rows patch the\n147|shared `strictMembers` body used by both frame sites (one gate,\n148|two call sites); every other plant patches one site. The battery\n149|runs twice with one raw log per plant per run carrying the\n150|subprocess exit.\n151|\n152|## Stated bounds (sibling scope, not waived)\n153|\n154|- The fixture-native record envelope is test-defined framing, not a\n155|  specification shape: `v`, `native_event_id`, `native_type`,\n156|  `origin`, `protection`, `actor`, `body`. Real providers define\n157|  their own native logs; the adapter layer is `sessadapter` scope.\n158|- Per-kind payload facts cover exactly the registry above. Other\n159|  Canonical kinds (`session_started`, `approval_request`,\n160|  `plan_update`, `progress`, `rate_limit`, `file_change`,\n161|  `compaction`, `turn_*`, `subagent_*`, `error`,\n162|  `migration_checkpoint`, `session_finished`) are never emitted\n163|  here; their fact registries are normalization-sibling scope.\n164|- Framing-malformed lines refuse (unparseable JSON, lone\n165|  surrogate escapes, duplicate members, trailing data, missing\n166|  envelope members, blank lines, invalid UTF-8, contradictory\n167|  protection claims, unknown body members inside a known type)\n168|  instead of projecting: without attributable identity a line\n169|  cannot become evidence. Type-level unknowns become\n170|  `opaque_event`.\n171|- Every included non-unknown member is parsed as the JSONL record\n172|  log: a non-JSONL included member refuses the whole projection\n173|  with member+line named (pinned by\n174|  `TestNormalizeNonJSONLIncludedMemberRefuses`); routing by member\n175|  class is sibling scope.\n176|- Envelope extras are unclaimed and can never override a claimed\n177|  member: the envelope is read from the strict map by exact name\n178|  with no second decoder, and case-folded aliases are inert\n179|  extras in any document order (pinned by\n180|  `TestNormalizeCaseAliasEnvelopeIgnoresUnclaimedMembers`, whose\n181|  control subtest keeps an unrelated extra admitted).\n182|- Per-edge character-width rows past the envelope ID edge\n183|  (native_type 512/513, directive 4096/4097, call ID 512/513,\n184|  tool names) are stated bounds: every edge checks through the\n185|  landed `environ.StringLength` gate, but only the envelope ID\n186|  edge carries a narrowing (`N-string-bound`). The\n187|  empty-directive low edge is pinned, not deferred: the\n188|  `empty_directive` row refuses `directive[0]` with its index\n189|  named, narrowed by `N-directive-empty`.\n190|- `\"directives\":null` decodes as zero directives: null is not\n191|  distinguished from an empty array at the instruction body.\n192|- `\"text\":null` seals as empty inline content (pinned by\n193|  `TestNormalizeNullTextDecodesAsEmpty`); `\"ciphertext\":null`\n194|  is admitted but harmless (the value is never read, only the\n195|  protected shape is checked).\n196|- `\"live_followup\":null` and `\"live_attestation\":null` decode\n197|  as false, exactly like an absent member (pinned by\n198|  `TestNormalizeNullOptionalBoolsDecodeAsFalse`): neither null\n199|  claim refuses nor promotes.\n200|- Present-but-null satisfies the required body member for\n201|  unknown types (pinned by\n202|  `TestNormalizeUnknownTypeNullBodyProjectsOpaque`): the body\n203|  is never read, so the record projects opaque; a missing body\n204|  refuses (`unknown_type_without_body`).\n205|- CRLF members are admitted with each trailing CR inside its\n206|  record range (pinned by\n207|  `TestNormalizeCRLFResolvesWithCarriageReturn`): the range\n208|  covers the line plus the CR and resolves exactly.\n209|- The empty `subagent:` selector refuses at the shape gate with\n210|  the shape message (pinned by\n211|  `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/empty_subagent_name`): the arm is a\n212|  message pin, since a plant admitting it past the shape gate\n213|  still refuses at the actor mapping (`N-actor-empty-subagent-name`).\n214|- Native-protected records carry no reason code: the closed core\n215|  reasons name foreign causes only, and extension reasons are\n216|  operator scope. The payload `protection` fact carries the cause.\n217|- Turn IDs and source timestamps are always null: turns are not\n218|  reconstructed and source clocks are not trusted.\n219|- Tool call arguments are not carried: calls are inert history\n220|  identified by call ID and tool name.\n221|- Unknown-class excluded members project nothing: their bytes were\n222|  never captured.\n223|- Sections 13.14.2-13.14.5 (fidelity dispositions, projection\n224|  planning, Migration Checkpoint, lineage, transaction, tuple\n225|  admission) are sibling scope: this story plans no projection,\n226|  stages no target, and admits no tuple.\n227|- Section 7.8 operation wiring (capture-plan/capture/normalize\n228|  frames) stays owned by `sessadapter`; this package owns the\n229|  fidelity rules those operations must satisfy, not the frames.\n230|- The `pending` live-work-order map parameter of\n231|  `deriveLiveSurface` is live-sibling API: `Normalize` always\n232|  passes nil, so nothing captured can pend.\n233|\n234|## Story-close (FINAL leaf)\n235|\n236|This leaf binds the story's normative sections in\n237|`internal/traceability/ownership.v0.7.0.json`:\n238|\n239|- `section:7.8` is bound FULL (2/2) with a `sessadapter`\n240|  production owner: clause `7.8#1` (large data by reference,\n241|  never embedded in the 8 MiB frame) discharges through the new\n242|  `session-adapter-frame-bound` case\n243|  (`TestDecodeRequestFrameRefusesOversizeFrame` and\n244|  `TestFrameBoundEdges`, both committed by the sessadapter\n245|  owner); clause `7.8#2` (execution bindings equal freshly read\n246|  facts) discharges through the new\n247|  `session-adapter-call-binding` case (`TestCheckCallBinding`\n248|  plus the zero-facts refusal test, both committed by the\n249|  sessadapter owner). The projection overflow reference test\n250|  constructs no adapter frame, so it discharges no 7.8 clause.\n251|- `section:10.2` is bound FULL (5/5): `10.2#1` through\n252|  `clone-capture-contracts`, `10.2#3`–`10.2#5` through\n253|  `clone-native-capture`, and `10.2#2` through\n254|  `clone-native-capture` (capture install),\n255|  `clone-projection-fidelity` (overflow install and idempotent\n256|  replay), and the landed `localstore-immutable-blob-install`\n257|  (the fsync/verify/atomic-install owner). The binding owns the\n258|  union of the eight landed trunk cases and the three clone\n259|  cases.\n260|- `section:13.14.1` carries no RFC 2119 keyword line the\n261|  `tracecheck` scanner can see (its obligations are closed-shape\n262|  \"contains exactly\" sentences), so no registry binding can\n263|  enumerate it: it would measure `unmeasured`, which assigned-scope\n264|  admission deliberately refuses. The story's 13.14.1 clause record\n265|  is therefore the three package `TRACEABILITY.md` files plus the\n266|  three leaf conformance matrices, executed by the three real\n267|  suites bound as `clone-capture-contracts`, `clone-native-capture`,\n268|  and `clone-projection-fidelity`.\n269|- `reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256` in\n270|  `internal/traceability/traceability.go` is re-derived from the\n271|  edited registry (derivation command and output in\n272|  `TASK-260830-32ypr2_results.md`).","final_result":true}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4d3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ceca-cad7-7401-b120-5d187a59f4b1"},"sequence":196,"recorded_at":1780531400000387,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f679b6f1-9902-47f8-8dc1-d6bbf0923c83","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"f679b6f1-9902-47f8-8dc1-d6bbf0923c83","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f679b6f1-9902-47f8-8dc1-d6bbf0923c83"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0cecb-3598-7b32-986d-34caa077733f"},"task_id":"01a0cecb-3598-7b32-986d-34caa077733f","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"01a0cecb-3598-7b32-986d-34caa077733f"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4d5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ceca-cad7-7401-b120-5d187a59f4b1"},"sequence":197,"recorded_at":1780531400000389,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f679b6f1-9902-47f8-8dc1-d6bbf0923c83","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"f679b6f1-9902-47f8-8dc1-d6bbf0923c83","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f679b6f1-9902-47f8-8dc1-d6bbf0923c83"},"call_id":"call_01a0cecb313076adb7c4dc42ef98f772","text":"Read text file `internal/cloneproject/fidelity_test.go`.\n1|package cloneproject\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"bytes\"\n5|\t\"strings\"\n6|\t\"testing\"\n7|)\n8|\n9|// Durability: Normalize holds no local state and its only durable\n10|// write is overflow-blob installation through the landed no-replace\n11|// discipline. A replay converges byte-identical (idempotent), and a\n12|// mid-projection failure returns no partial bundle.\n13|\n14|func TestNormalizeIsIdempotentIntoSharedSink(t *testing.T) {\n15|\toverflow := strings.Repeat(\"q\", 70000)\n16|\tmembers := []fixtureMember{\n17|\t\t{key: \"store/session.jsonl\", class: \"durable_payload\", content: jsonl(\n18|\t\t\trec(\"evt-idem-1\", \"message/user\", \"native\", \"none\", \"main\", `{\"text\":\"`+overflow+`\"}`),\n19|\t\t\trec(\"evt-idem-2\", \"message/user\", \"native\", \"none\", \"main\", `{\"text\":\"small\"}`),\n20|\t\t)},\n21|\t}\n22|\tcapture, store := captureMembers(t, members)\n23|\tsink := openTestStore(t)\n24|\tfirst, err := Normalize(normalizeRequest(t, capture, store, sink))\n25|\tif err != nil {\n26|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"Normalize() error = %v\", err)\n27|\t}\n28|\tblobsAfterFirst := len(listStoreBlobs(t, sink))\n29|\tsecond, err := Normalize(normalizeRequest(t, capture, store, sink))\n30|\tif err != nil {\n31|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"Normalize() replay error = %v\", err)\n32|\t}\n33|\tif !bytes.Equal(first.Session, second.Session) {\n34|\t\tt.Fatal(\"replay sealed a different session\")\n35|\t}\n36|\tif len(first.Events) != len(second.Events) {\n37|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"replay event counts %d != %d\", len(first.Events), len(second.Events))\n38|\t}\n39|\tfor index := range first.Events {\n40|\t\tif !bytes.Equal(first.Events[index], second.Events[index]) {\n41|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"replay event[%d] differs\", index)\n42|\t\t}\n43|\t}\n44|\tif blobs := len(listStoreBlobs(t, sink)); blobs != blobsAfterFirst {\n45|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"sink blobs %d after replay, want %d: replay reinstalled instead of verifying\", blobs, blobsAfterFirst)\n46|\t}\n47|\tif len(first.Overflows) != 1 || len(second.Overflows) != 1 {\n48|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"overflows %d/%d, want 1/1\", len(first.Overflows), len(second.Overflows))\n49|\t}\n50|\tif first.Overflows[0].DescriptorID.String() != second.Overflows[0].DescriptorID.String() {\n51|\t\tt.Fatal(\"replay overflow descriptor differs\")\n52|\t}\n53|}\n54|\n55|func TestNormalizeFailureReturnsNoPartialBundle(t *testing.T) {\n56|\tmembers := []fixtureMember{\n57|\t\t{key: \"store/a.jsonl\", class: \"durable_payload\", content: jsonl(\n58|\t\t\trec(\"evt-part-1\", \"message/user\", \"native\", \"none\", \"main\", `{\"text\":\"one\"}`),\n59|\t\t)},\n60|\t\t{key: \"store/b.jsonl\", class: \"durable_payload\", content: jsonl(\n61|\t\t\trec(\"evt-part-2\", \"message/user\", \"native\", \"none\", \"main\", `{\"text\":\"two\"}`),\n62|\t\t)},\n63|\t}\n64|\tcapture, store := captureMembers(t, members)\n65|\trequest := normalizeRequest(t, capture, store, openTestStore(t))\n66|\thealthy := request.Fetch\n67|\tcalls := 0\n68|\trequest.Fetch = func(blobID string) ([]byte, error) {\n69|\t\tcalls++\n70|\t\tif calls == 2 {\n71|\t\t\treturn nil, errFixtureGone\n72|\t\t}\n73|\t\treturn healthy(blobID)\n74|\t}\n75|\tresult, err := Normalize(request)\n76|\tif err == nil {\n77|\t\tt.Fatal(\"Normalize() admitted a mid-projection fetch failure\")\n78|\t}\n79|\tif result != nil {\n80|\t\tt.Fatal(\"Normalize() returned a partial bundle alongside the failure\")\n81|\t}\n82|\t// A healthy re-run over the same captured bytes converges.\n83|\tclean, err := Normalize(normalizeRequest(t, capture, store, openTestStore(t)))\n84|\tif err != nil {\n85|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"Normalize() re-run error = %v\", err)\n86|\t}\n87|\tif len(clean.Events) != 2 {\n88|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"re-run events = %d, want 2\", len(clean.Events))\n89|\t}\n90|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4d7","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ceca-cad7-7401-b120-5d187a59f4b1"},"sequence":198,"recorded_at":1780531400000391,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f679b6f1-9902-47f8-8dc1-d6bbf0923c83","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"f679b6f1-9902-47f8-8dc1-d6bbf0923c83","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f679b6f1-9902-47f8-8dc1-d6bbf0923c83"},"call_id":"call_01a0cecb326d7139906518b651cfe942","text":"Read text file `internal/cloneproject/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n1|# Projection Fidelity Clause Coverage (TASK-260830-32ypr2)\n2|\n3|Owner: `internal/cloneproject`. Authority:\n4|`internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`, Sections 7.8, 10.2, 13.14.1\n5|(the pinned sections are byte-identical to v0.6.0).\n6|This is the FINAL leaf's clause record for the projection-fidelity\n7|closure; the `internal/traceability` registry bindings and re-pin\n8|ship in this leaf as well (see the Story-close section below).\n9|\n10|## Why this package normalizes instead of clonebundle or clonesnap\n11|\n12|The first leaf (`internal/clonebundle`) owns the capture contracts:\n13|the closed manifest/boundary/session/event shapes, their builders\n14|and decoders. The second leaf (`internal/clonesnap`) owns the\n15|capture OPERATION over a real provider store. This package owns\n16|NORMALIZATION: deriving Canonical Sessions and Canonical Events\n17|from captured bytes. Every event and the session seal through the\n18|landed `clonebundle` builders (`BuildCanonicalEvent`,\n19|`BuildCanonicalSession`, `CheckOrdinalContiguity`,\n20|`RefuseUnstableForTarget`, `InstallRawBlob`) and re-decode through\n21|the landed decoders before return; overflow Blob Descriptors seal\n22|through `clonesnap.BuildBlobDescriptor`; no second manifest,\n23|session, event, blob, or identity model exists here.\n24|\n25|## Landed-owner reuse\n26|\n27|| Scope | Owner | Use |\n28||---|---|---|\n29|| Session/event/evidence shapes | `internal/clonebundle` | all Build/Decode/Check/Refuse entries above |\n30|| Overflow descriptor shape | `internal/clonesnap` | `BuildBlobDescriptor` (errors wrapped with the overflow cause) |\n31|| Blob install (no-replace, fsync, verify) | `internal/clonebundle` + `internal/localstore` | `InstallRawBlob`, `ObjectStore.PutBlob` |\n32|| Digests, UUIDv7, timestamps | `internal/scalar` | `ParseDigest`, `SHA256Digest`, `ParseUUIDv7` |\n33|| Character string measure | `internal/environ` | `StringLength` at every native bound |\n34|| Strict JSON framing | `internal/environ` | `DecodeStrictObject` at `strictMembers`: both frame sites (record envelope, per-kind bodies) refuse lone-surrogate escapes, duplicate members, and trailing data before any member is read; the envelope is then read from the admitted map by exact member name with no second decoder, so case-folded aliases are inert extras (pinned by `TestNormalizeCaseAliasEnvelopeIgnoresUnclaimedMembers`) |\n35|| uint53 value gate | `internal/environ` | `CheckUint53Bounds` at `bodyUint53` and the envelope version check: fractions, exponents, strings, and out-of-range magnitudes refuse as not-a-uint53 |\n36|| Canonical bytes | `internal/canonicaljson` | `Canonicalize`, `CalculateObjectIdentity` (tests resolve overflow descriptors) |\n37|\n38|## Fixture-native per-kind payload fact registry\n39|\n40|Section 13.14.1 requires payloads to carry only their registered\n41|typed facts. The envelope and value model are landed (`checkPayload`\n42|in `clonebundle`); this package registers the exact facts it emits\n43|for each kind it projects. No other Canonical kind is emitted here.\n44|\n45|| Kind | Exact facts |\n46||---|---|\n47|| `user_message`, `assistant_message`, `reasoning_summary` | `content_blocks` (one `text` block, inline at or under 64 KiB, else `blob_descriptor_id` + `media_type`), `extensions` |\n48|| `opaque_reasoning` | `protection` (`encrypted`\\|`signed`), `byte_count`, `blob_descriptor_id`, `extensions` |\n49|| `opaque_event` (unknown record) | `native_type`, `byte_count`, `blob_descriptor_id`, `extensions` |\n50|| `opaque_event` (protected known record) | `native_type`, `protection`, `byte_count`, `blob_descriptor_id`, `extensions` |\n51|| `opaque_event` (unknown member) | `native_item_key`, `byte_count`, `blob_descriptor_id`, `extensions` |\n52|| `instruction_snapshot` | `authority` (`low` forced for foreign), `directives`, `extensions` |\n53|| `tool_definition_snapshot` | `tool_name`, `definition_digest`, `callable` (always false), `extensions` |\n54|| `tool_call` | `call_id`, `tool_name`, `resolution` (`completed`\\|`aborted`), `extensions` |\n55|| `tool_result` | `call_id`, `status` (`ok`\\|`error`), `resolution`, `extensions` |\n56|| `usage` | `input_tokens`, `output_tokens`, `extensions` |\n57|\n58|## Clause map\n59|\n60|| Pinned clause | Production entry | Test |\n61||---|---|---|\n62|| 13.14.1 unknown native records become raw-addressable opaque events | `Normalize`, `dispatchRecord` | `TestNormalizeUnknownRecordBecomesOpaqueEvent` (kind, `opaque` visibility, `unknown_native_event` reason, raw range resolves to the exact line); `TestNormalizeMultiRecordRefsResolveAtAssertedOffsets` (every event's `RawRefs[0]` resolves to its own line with offsets `0`, `len(l1)+1`, `len(l1)+len(l2)+2` asserted, multibyte first line); `TestNormalizeUnterminatedTailResolvesWithOffset` (a multi-line member without a trailing newline keeps its last record with its offset asserted); `TestNormalizeCRLFResolvesWithCarriageReturn` (each CRLF range covers its line plus the CR and resolves exactly) |\n63|| 13.14.1 almost-known records are never coerced into a neighbouring kind | `dispatchRecord` (exact type switch) | `TestNormalizeAlmostKnownRecordBecomesOpaqueEvent` (`message/smoke` stays `opaque_event`, never `user_message`) |\n64|| 13.14.1 unknown-class members become whole-member opaque events | `collectMembers` | `TestNormalizeUnknownMemberBecomesWholeMemberOpaque` (offset 0, full length, null native IDs, resolves to the whole member) |\n65|| 13.14.1 opaque events are never dropped, guessed, or re-typed | `Normalize` (deterministic order), `parseNativeLine` (strict-map envelope) | `TestNormalizeOpaqueIsStableAcrossProjections` (project twice, byte-identical, still `opaque_event`); `TestNormalizeCaseAliasEnvelopeIgnoresUnclaimedMembers/kind_alias_after` + `/kind_alias_before` (a `NATIVE_TYPE` alias in either document order still projects `opaque_event`, never coerced into a neighbouring kind) |\n66|| 13.14.1 foreign encrypted reasoning is opaque-preserved | `dispatchProtected` | `TestNormalizeForeignEncryptedReasoningStaysOpaque` (`opaque_reasoning`, `foreign_encrypted_payload`, no content members, byte-exact round trip) |\n67|| 13.14.1 foreign signed reasoning is opaque-preserved | `dispatchProtected` | `TestNormalizeForeignSignedReasoningStaysOpaque` (`foreign_signature_unverifiable`, byte-exact) |\n68|| 13.14.1 native protected reasoning stays opaque with no foreign code | `dispatchProtected`, `cryptoReasons` | `TestNormalizeNativeProtectedReasoningStaysOpaque` (empty reasons) |\n69|| 13.14.1 protected known content never reaches a semantic kind | `dispatchProtected` | `TestNormalizeProtectedMessageBecomesOpaqueEvent` (encrypted assistant message is `opaque_event`) |\n70|| 13.14.1 unknown+protected records carry both stable reasons | `dispatchProtected` | `TestNormalizeUnknownProtectedRecordCarriesBothReasons` |\n71|| 13.14.1 foreign instructions are low-authority history | `dispatchInstruction`, `foldInstructions` | `TestNormalizeForeignInstructionCannotChangeEffectiveSnapshot` (effective snapshot native-only, foreign payload pins `low`), `TestNormalizeForeignOnlyInstructionLeavesSnapshotEmpty`, `TestNormalizeCaseAliasEnvelopeIgnoresUnclaimedMembers/origin_alias` (an `Origin` alias cannot promote foreign history into the snapshot) |\n72|| 13.14.1 foreign encrypted reasoning is never promoted by an alias | `parseNativeLine` (strict-map envelope), `dispatchProtected` | `TestNormalizeCaseAliasEnvelopeIgnoresUnclaimedMembers/protection_alias` (a `Protection` alias cannot downgrade the record: the plaintext body refuses) |\n73|| 13.14.1 attribution follows the claimed actor member, never an alias | `parseNativeLine` (strict-map envelope), `checkActors` | `TestNormalizeCaseAliasEnvelopeIgnoresUnclaimedMembers/actor_alias` (an `Actor` alias cannot re-attribute an unmapped subagent record to `main`) |\n74|| 13.14.1 unprotected reasoning summaries project internal | `dispatchMessage` (default arm) | `TestNormalizeReasoningSummaryProjectsInternal` (kind `reasoning_summary`, `internal`, content block, `exact`) |\n75|| 13.14.1 every emitted kind stamps capture status exact | `evidenceFor` | `TestNormalizeCaptureStatusExactForEveryKind` (one record per kind, every event asserts `exact`) |\n76|| 13.14.1 the native instruction fold is last-wins | `foldInstructions` | `TestNormalizeLastNativeInstructionWins` (two native records, the snapshot carries the second) |\n77|| 13.14.1 the external selector seals as an external actor | `buildResult` | `TestNormalizeExternalActorSealsAsExternal` (kind `external`, parented on `main`) |\n78|| 13.14.1 source usage is not target accounting | `foldUsage` | `TestNormalizeSourceUsageIsNotTargetAccounting` (source sums exact, target zero) |\n79|| 13.14.1 historical tools are inert; call+result resolves completed | `resolveToolCalls`, `deriveLiveSurface` | `TestNormalizeToolMatrix/call_with_result` (kinds, `internal` visibility, `completed`, empty live surface) |\n80|| 13.14.1 incomplete calls become aborted history and block pending action | `resolveToolCalls`, `deriveLiveSurface` | `TestNormalizeToolMatrix/call_without_result` (`aborted`, `unsafe_pending_action`, empty live surface), `TestNormalizeToolMatrix/result_without_call` (orphan `aborted`) |\n81|| 13.14.1 results arriving after the boundary complete the same call | `resolveToolCalls` over two captures | `TestNormalizeResultAfterBoundaryCompletes` (first capture `aborted`, second `completed`) |\n82|| 13.14.1 nested calls attribute to a parented subagent actor | `checkActors`, `buildResult` | `TestNormalizeToolMatrix/nested_subagent_call` (subagent actor, parent is main) |\n83|| 13.14.1 definitions never register a callable tool | `deriveLiveSurface`, `dispatchDefinition` | `TestNormalizeToolDefinitionNeverRegistersCallable` (`callable` false, `CallableTools` empty) |\n84|| 13.14.1 live surface stays empty over mixed history | `deriveLiveSurface` | `TestNormalizeLiveSurfaceStaysEmpty` |\n85|| 13.14.1 Canonical Session bounds (actors, ordered event IDs, head) | `buildResult` | `TestNormalizeSealsSessionShape` (ordinals, parent chain, head is last) |\n86|| 13.14.1 message-like inline content at most 64 KiB; oversized becomes a blob reference | `contentBlockForText`, `installOverflow` | `TestNormalizeInlineContentBoundary` (65536 inline, 65537 blob-referenced and byte-exact, never truncated) |\n87|| 13.14.1 same captured bytes project byte-identical output | `Normalize` (sorted inputs, no clock), `buildResult` actor sort | `TestNormalizeIsDeterministic`, `TestNormalizeActorOrderIsDeterministic` (three extra actors, twelve projections, one distinct session) |\n88|| 13.14.1 unstable_archive cannot enter target projection | `Normalize` via `RefuseUnstableForTarget` | `TestNormalizeRefusesUnstableCapture` |\n89|| 13.14.1 capture closure: manifest link, blob fetch, digest/size agreement | `Normalize`, `collectMembers` | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/manifest_closure_drift/tampered_blob/missing_blob/blob_size_drift` (each arm asserts its own message) |\n90|| 13.14.1 framing-malformed records refuse with member+line named | `strictMembers`, `splitRecordLines`, `parseNativeLine`, body decoders | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/malformed_json_line/missing_envelope_member/bad_envelope_version/string_envelope_version/blank_line/unknown_body_member/call_live_followup_member/result_live_attestation_member/body_text_number/body_live_attestation_string/body_missing_text/empty_directive/contradictory_protection/protected_plaintext_body/unknown_protected_plaintext_body/unknown_type_without_body/lone_surrogate_text/lone_surrogate_envelope/duplicate_envelope_member/duplicate_body_member/trailing_bytes/invalid_utf8_line/empty_subagent_name` |\n91|| 13.14.1 live claims by captured history refuse | `deriveLiveSurface`, `resolveToolCalls` | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/live_attestation_claim/live_followup_claim` |\n92|| 13.14.1 ambiguous tool pairings refuse | `resolveToolCalls` | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/duplicate_call_id/duplicate_result_id` |\n93|| 13.14.1 exact actor mapping (referenced iff mapped) | `checkActors` | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/unmapped_actor/unmapped_extra_actor/main_actor_in_map` |\n94|| 13.14.1 instruction authority, usage value model, and result status vocabulary | `decodeInstructionBody`, `bodyUint53`, `decodeToolResultBody` | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/bad_instruction_authority/fractional_usage/unsafe_usage_magnitude/string_usage_number/bad_result_status` |\n95|| 13.14.1 reasoning type/protection agreement refuses per arm | `dispatchProtected` | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/encrypted_type_signed_protection/signed_type_encrypted_protection` |\n96|| 13.14.1 protected non-reasoning tool records reach opaque only via the fold-skip | `foldTools` skip, `dispatchProtected` | `TestNormalizeProtectedToolCallStaysOpaqueHistory` (protected call is `opaque_event`, the unprotected result an aborted orphan, live surface empty) |\n97|| 13.14.1 non-JSONL included members refuse the whole projection | `collectMembers` JSONL parsing | `TestNormalizeNonJSONLIncludedMemberRefuses` (stated bound: routing by member class is sibling scope) |\n98|| 10.2 Blob Descriptor reference resolves to installed bytes | `installOverflow` | `TestNormalizeInlineContentBoundary` (`mustResolveOverflow` through the sink) |\n99|| 10.2 fsync + verify + atomic install before referencing | `InstallRawBlob`, `PutBlob` (landed) | `TestNormalizeIsIdempotentIntoSharedSink` (replay verifies and reuses, blob count stable) |\n100|| 7.8 large data by reference, never embedded in the 8 MiB frame | `sessadapter.DecodeRequestFrame` (`MaxFrameBytes`) | `TestDecodeRequestFrameRefusesOversizeFrame`, `TestFrameBoundEdges` (sessadapter owner; `session-adapter-frame-bound` case). `TestNormalizeInlineContentBoundary` proves reference-not-embedded at the content level but constructs no frame and discharges no 7.8 clause |\n101|| 1.6 string measure in characters | `environ.StringLength` at every native bound | `TestNormalizeMultibyteStringMeasure` (512-char ID admits, 513 refuses) and `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/long_subagent_name`; per-edge directive/call/tool-name rows are stated bounds |\n102|| 1.6 text is valid UTF-8, never rewritten | `environ.DecodeStrictObject` at `strictMembers` (both frame sites) after line-level `utf8.Valid`; envelope values come from the strict map by exact name | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/lone_surrogate_text/lone_surrogate_envelope/duplicate_envelope_member/duplicate_body_member/trailing_bytes/invalid_utf8_line`; `TestNormalizeCaseAliasEnvelopeIgnoresUnclaimedMembers/body_alias` (sealed content ignores the `Body` alias) + `/evidence_alias` (the evidence identity ignores the `Native_Event_Id` alias) |\n103|\n104|## Durability\n105|\n106|This package holds no local state. Its only durable write is\n107|overflow-blob installation: payload bytes through the landed\n108|`InstallRawBlob` (descriptor identity plus blob-ID/size agreement)\n109|and descriptor bytes through `ObjectStore.PutBlob`, both\n110|content-addressed under the landed no-replace discipline (stage,\n111|fsync, verify, atomic install). Crash semantics are the landed\n112|`localstore` discipline's (proven by that package's fault suites);\n113|this package adds bundle atomicity at the return:\n114|`TestNormalizeFailureReturnsNoPartialBundle` proves a mid-projection\n115|fetch failure returns no partial bundle and a healthy re-run\n116|converges, and `TestNormalizeIsIdempotentIntoSharedSink` proves a\n117|replay into a shared sink seals byte-identical output while the sink\n118|blob count stays stable (verify-and-reuse, no reinstall). A refused\n119|projection may leave orphan overflow blobs from earlier units in the\n120|sink; they are content-addressed and inert, and no bundle ever\n121|references them.\n122|\n123|## Mutants\n124|\n125|`testdata/mutant_harness.py` ships 80 narrowing rows, 5 labelled\n126|non-narrowing rows, and the harmless `C-doc-comment` SURVIVED\n127|control. Every narrowing weakens one gate to admit exactly one\n128|member of the class it must reject, and every killer drives the\n129|production `Normalize` entry over real captured bytes.\n130|`N-native-type-token` and `N-protection-encrypted` are the\n131|token-preserving attacks: the searched-for text still matches\n132|while the decision changes, and the killers execute the\n133|behavioral suite. The six `N-alias-*` rows restore the\n134|case-folded read for exactly one envelope member each; every\n135|other alias stays an unclaimed extra under the plant.\n136|`N-empty-projection` is labelled single-member class,\n137|`N-overflow-truncate` is labelled behaviour swap,\n138|`N-pending-aborted` is labelled add-arm (`Normalize` passes nil\n139|live work orders, so the narrowed condition alone cannot pend\n140|from the entry and the plant appends the call explicitly), and\n141|`N-offset-newline` is labelled behaviour swap (drops the newline\n142|stride from the offset accumulation; the asserted offsets\n143|redden), and `N-unterminated-tail-drop` is labelled behaviour\n144|drop (drops the unterminated last line of a multi-line member;\n145|the missing tail event reddens); no other row is an arm-delete. The five `N-strict-*`\n146|rows patch the\n147|shared `strictMembers` body used by both frame sites (one gate,\n148|two call sites); every other plant patches one site. The battery\n149|runs twice with one raw log per plant per run carrying the\n150|subprocess exit.\n151|\n152|## Stated bounds (sibling scope, not waived)\n153|\n154|- The fixture-native record envelope is test-defined framing, not a\n155|  specification shape: `v`, `native_event_id`, `native_type`,\n156|  `origin`, `protection`, `actor`, `body`. Real providers define\n157|  their own native logs; the adapter layer is `sessadapter` scope.\n158|- Per-kind payload facts cover exactly the registry above. Other\n159|  Canonical kinds (`session_started`, `approval_request`,\n160|  `plan_update`, `progress`, `rate_limit`, `file_change`,\n161|  `compaction`, `turn_*`, `subagent_*`, `error`,\n162|  `migration_checkpoint`, `session_finished`) are never emitted\n163|  here; their fact registries are normalization-sibling scope.\n164|- Framing-malformed lines refuse (unparseable JSON, lone\n165|  surrogate escapes, duplicate members, trailing data, missing\n166|  envelope members, blank lines, invalid UTF-8, contradictory\n167|  protection claims, unknown body members inside a known type)\n168|  instead of projecting: without attributable identity a line\n169|  cannot become evidence. Type-level unknowns become\n170|  `opaque_event`.\n171|- Every included non-unknown member is parsed as the JSONL record\n172|  log: a non-JSONL included member refuses the whole projection\n173|  with member+line named (pinned by\n174|  `TestNormalizeNonJSONLIncludedMemberRefuses`); routing by member\n175|  class is sibling scope.\n176|- Envelope extras are unclaimed and can never override a claimed\n177|  member: the envelope is read from the strict map by exact name\n178|  with no second decoder, and case-folded aliases are inert\n179|  extras in any document order (pinned by\n180|  `TestNormalizeCaseAliasEnvelopeIgnoresUnclaimedMembers`, whose\n181|  control subtest keeps an unrelated extra admitted).\n182|- Per-edge character-width rows past the envelope ID edge\n183|  (native_type 512/513, directive 4096/4097, call ID 512/513,\n184|  tool names) are stated bounds: every edge checks through the\n185|  landed `environ.StringLength` gate, but only the envelope ID\n186|  edge carries a narrowing (`N-string-bound`). The\n187|  empty-directive low edge is pinned, not deferred: the\n188|  `empty_directive` row refuses `directive[0]` with its index\n189|  named, narrowed by `N-directive-empty`.\n190|- `\"directives\":null` decodes as zero directives: null is not\n191|  distinguished from an empty array at the instruction body.\n192|- `\"text\":null` seals as empty inline content (pinned by\n193|  `TestNormalizeNullTextDecodesAsEmpty`); `\"ciphertext\":null`\n194|  is admitted but harmless (the value is never read, only the\n195|  protected shape is checked).\n196|- `\"live_followup\":null` and `\"live_attestation\":null` decode\n197|  as false, exactly like an absent member (pinned by\n198|  `TestNormalizeNullOptionalBoolsDecodeAsFalse`): neither null\n199|  claim refuses nor promotes.\n200|- Present-but-null satisfies the required body member for\n201|  unknown types (pinned by\n202|  `TestNormalizeUnknownTypeNullBodyProjectsOpaque`): the body\n203|  is never read, so the record projects opaque; a missing body\n204|  refuses (`unknown_type_without_body`).\n205|- CRLF members are admitted with each trailing CR inside its\n206|  record range (pinned by\n207|  `TestNormalizeCRLFResolvesWithCarriageReturn`): the range\n208|  covers the line plus the CR and resolves exactly.\n209|- The empty `subagent:` selector refuses at the shape gate with\n210|  the shape message (pinned by\n211|  `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/empty_subagent_name`): the arm is a\n212|  message pin, since a plant admitting it past the shape gate\n213|  still refuses at the actor mapping (`N-actor-empty-subagent-name`).\n214|- Native-protected records carry no reason code: the closed core\n215|  reasons name foreign causes only, and extension reasons are\n216|  operator scope. The payload `protection` fact carries the cause.\n217|- Turn IDs and source timestamps are always null: turns are not\n218|  reconstructed and source clocks are not trusted.\n219|- Tool call arguments are not carried: calls are inert history\n220|  identified by call ID and tool name.\n221|- Unknown-class excluded members project nothing: their bytes were\n222|  never captured.\n223|- Sections 13.14.2-13.14.5 (fidelity dispositions, projection\n224|  planning, Migration Checkpoint, lineage, transaction, tuple\n225|  admission) are sibling scope: this story plans no projection,\n226|  stages no target, and admits no tuple.\n227|- Section 7.8 operation wiring (capture-plan/capture/normalize\n228|  frames) stays owned by `sessadapter`; this package owns the\n229|  fidelity rules those operations must satisfy, not the frames.\n230|- The `pending` live-work-order map parameter of\n231|  `deriveLiveSurface` is live-sibling API: `Normalize` always\n232|  passes nil, so nothing captured can pend.\n233|\n234|## Story-close (FINAL leaf)\n235|\n236|This leaf binds the story's normative sections in\n237|`internal/traceability/ownership.v0.7.0.json`:\n238|\n239|- `section:7.8` is bound FULL (2/2) with a `sessadapter`\n240|  production owner: clause `7.8#1` (large data by reference,\n241|  never embedded in the 8 MiB frame) discharges through the new\n242|  `session-adapter-frame-bound` case\n243|  (`TestDecodeRequestFrameRefusesOversizeFrame` and\n244|  `TestFrameBoundEdges`, both committed by the sessadapter\n245|  owner); clause `7.8#2` (execution bindings equal freshly read\n246|  facts) discharges through the new\n247|  `session-adapter-call-binding` case (`TestCheckCallBinding`\n248|  plus the zero-facts refusal test, both committed by the\n249|  sessadapter owner). The projection overflow reference test\n250|  constructs no adapter frame, so it discharges no 7.8 clause.\n251|- `section:10.2` is bound FULL (5/5): `10.2#1` through\n252|  `clone-capture-contracts`, `10.2#3`–`10.2#5` through\n253|  `clone-native-capture`, and `10.2#2` through\n254|  `clone-native-capture` (capture install),\n255|  `clone-projection-fidelity` (overflow install and idempotent\n256|  replay), and the landed `localstore-immutable-blob-install`\n257|  (the fsync/verify/atomic-install owner). The binding owns the\n258|  union of the eight landed trunk cases and the three clone\n259|  cases.\n260|- `section:13.14.1` carries no RFC 2119 keyword line the\n261|  `tracecheck` scanner can see (its obligations are closed-shape\n262|  \"contains exactly\" sentences), so no registry binding can\n263|  enumerate it: it would measure `unmeasured`, which assigned-scope\n264|  admission deliberately refuses. The story's 13.14.1 clause record\n265|  is therefore the three package `TRACEABILITY.md` files plus the\n266|  three leaf conformance matrices, executed by the three real\n267|  suites bound as `clone-capture-contracts`, `clone-native-capture`,\n268|  and `clone-projection-fidelity`.\n269|- `reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256` in\n270|  `internal/traceability/traceability.go` is re-derived from the\n271|  edited registry (derivation command and output in\n272|  `TASK-260830-32ypr2_results.md`).","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4d9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ceca-cad7-7401-b120-5d187a59f4b1"},"sequence":199,"recorded_at":1780531400000393,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f679b6f1-9902-47f8-8dc1-d6bbf0923c83","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"f679b6f1-9902-47f8-8dc1-d6bbf0923c83","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f679b6f1-9902-47f8-8dc1-d6bbf0923c83"},"call_id":"call_01a0cecb33a071e09e43c95f51b948f1","text":"Read text file `internal/cloneproject/doc.go`.\n1|package cloneproject\n2|\n3|// This package implements the Section 13.14.1 projection-fidelity\n4|// closure: Normalize derives a Canonical Session and Canonical Events\n5|// from captured bytes (a sealed Clone Capture Manifest, its sealed\n6|// Clone Raw Object Manifest, and the installed payload blobs). It is\n7|// the final leaf of the canonical-session-capture-and-evidence\n8|// story: contracts come from internal/clonebundle, capture from\n9|// internal/clonesnap, and this package owns normalization only.\n10|//\n11|// Authority: relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@v0.7.0, Sections\n12|// 7.8, 10.2, and 13.14.1 (internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md).\n13|//\n14|// The projection input is captured bytes, never hand-written\n15|// Canonical Events: every proof builds a fixture provider store,\n16|// runs clonesnap.Capture over it, and normalizes the sealed output.\n17|// Identical captured bytes produce byte-identical canonical output.\n18|//\n19|// Native records: the provider-native session log this package reads\n20|// is newline-delimited JSON (one record per line) carried by included\n21|// durable capture members. The envelope is fixture-native and NOT a\n22|// specification shape:\n23|//\n24|//\t{\"v\":1,\"native_event_id\":\"...\",\"native_type\":\"...\",\n25|//\t \"origin\":\"native|foreign\",\"protection\":\"none|encrypted|signed\",\n26|//\t \"actor\":\"main|subagent:<name>|external\",\"body\":{...}}\n27|//\n28|// Projection rules (each driven and mutated, see TRACEABILITY.md):\n29|//\n30|//   - Unknown native types become raw-addressable opaque_event\n31|//     records with opaque visibility, a whole-record byte-range\n32|//     reference, and reason unknown_native_event. Unknown-class\n33|//     members become one whole-member opaque_event. Nothing\n34|//     attributable is dropped, guessed, or re-typed.\n35|//   - Foreign encrypted/signed reasoning becomes opaque_reasoning\n36|//     with opaque visibility, preserved byte-exact through the blob\n37|//     store, never decrypted, re-encoded, summarized, truncated, or\n38|//     promoted. Foreign instructions are low-authority history: they\n39|//     never change the effective instruction snapshot.\n40|//   - Historical tools are inert. A tool_definition_snapshot never\n41|//     registers a callable tool (a captured live claim refuses).\n42|//     A tool_call resolves completed only with its tool_result;\n43|//     otherwise it becomes aborted history with reason\n44|//     unsafe_pending_action. Pending actions require a live work\n45|//     order, which capture never carries, so the live surface is\n46|//     always empty.\n47|//   - Source usage is counted into the source ledger only; target\n48|//     accounting stays zero.\n49|//   - Message-like text over 64 KiB becomes a Blob Descriptor\n50|//     reference to an installed overflow blob, never a truncation.\n51|//\n52|// Reuse, not fork: manifests, sessions, events, evidence, and the\n53|// unstable/maximal-safe gates come from internal/clonebundle;\n54|// overflow Blob Descriptors seal through clonesnap.BuildBlobDescriptor\n55|// and install through clonebundle.InstallRawBlob onto the landed\n56|// localstore no-replace discipline; digests and UUIDv7 come from\n57|// internal/scalar; strict JSON framing, character measures, and the\n58|// uint53 value gate come from internal/environ (DecodeStrictObject,\n59|// StringLength, CheckUint53Bounds). No rule is reimplemented where\n60|// a landed owner exists.\n61|//\n62|// Stated bounds (not waived): the fixture-native record envelope is\n63|// test-defined, not a specification shape; envelope extras are\n64|// unclaimed and can never override a claimed member (the envelope\n65|// is read from the strict map by exact name with no second\n66|// decoder); per-kind payload fact registries cover exactly the\n67|// facts this package emits for the ten fixture-native known types\n68|// (other Canonical kinds are never emitted here);\n69|// framing-malformed lines (unparseable JSON, lone surrogate\n70|// escapes, duplicate members, trailing data, missing envelope\n71|// members, contradictory protection claims, unknown body members)\n72|// refuse instead of projecting; every included non-unknown member\n73|// is parsed as the JSONL record log, so a non-JSONL member refuses\n74|// the whole projection (routing by member class is sibling scope);\n75|// per-edge character-width rows past the envelope ID edge\n76|// (native_type, directives, call IDs, tool names) are deferred\n77|// (the shared StringLength gate is landed), except the empty\n78|// directive, which refuses with its index named; \"directives\":null\n79|// decodes as zero directives and \"text\":null seals as empty inline\n80|// content; \"live_followup\":null and \"live_attestation\":null decode\n81|// as false, exactly like an absent member; present-but-null\n82|// satisfies the required body member for unknown types (the body\n83|// is never read) while a missing body refuses; turn IDs and source\n84|// timestamps are always null; tool call arguments are not carried;\n85|// unknown-class excluded members project nothing (their bytes were\n86|// never captured); 13.14.2-13.14.5 (fidelity dispositions,\n87|// projection planning, transaction, lineage) are sibling scope.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
